					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="anom-bar-container item-5368 clear-3 keter none ekhi critical {$american}"> <div class="anom-bar"> <div class="top-box"> <div class="top-left-box"><span class="item">Item#:</span> <span class="number">5368</span></div> <div class="top-center-box"> <div class="bar-one"></div> <div class="bar-two"></div> <div class="bar-three"></div> <div class="bar-four"></div> <div class="bar-five"></div> <div class="bar-six"></div> </div> <div class="top-right-box"> <div class="level">Level3</div> <div class="clearance"></div> </div> </div> <div class="bottom-box"> <div class="text-part"> <div class="main-class"> <div class="contain-class"> <div class="class-category">Containment Class:</div> <div class="class-text">keter</div> </div> <div class="second-class"> <div class="class-category">Secondary Class:</div> <div class="class-text">none</div> </div> </div> <div class="disrupt-class"> <div class="class-category">Disruption Class:</div> <div class="class-text">ekhi</div> </div> <div class="risk-class"> <div class="class-category">Risk Class:</div> <div class="class-text">critical</div> </div> </div> <div class="diamond-part"> <div class="danger-diamond"><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/classification-committee-memo">link to memo</a><br /> <div class="arrows"></div> <div class="octagon"></div> <div class="quadrants"> <div class="top-quad"></div> <div class="right-quad"></div> <div class="left-quad"></div> <div class="bottom-quad"></div> </div> <div class="top-icon"></div> <div class="right-icon"></div> <div class="left-icon"></div> <div class="bottom-icon"></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5368 is in designated Site-318, a patch of desert located 500 miles south of El Alamein, Egypt. Any attempt to contact the asset without the approval of a Level-4 Clearance Member is restricted. MTF Epsilon-6, Gamma-5, and one mechanized battalion from the Egyptian army(if necessary, terminate them) must be on-site, and they must have tanks with electromagnetic cannons. Only authorized Class-B, Class-C, and Class-E personnel are allowed access to this location and must always have an armored division as an escort in case SCP-5368 becomes hostile. If this case occurs, flerovium gas will be applied and will pacify it until further notice.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5368-A is an entity that infused itself with Tiger tank 132, designated as SCP-5368-B. SCP-5368-A can utilize all of SCP-5368-B's system, including its 88&#160;mm cannon and 2× 7.92&#160;mm MG34. SCP-5368-A also apparently has some unique abilities and characteristics as the weapons and armor on SCP-5368-B seems to be enhanced, allowing better protection and firepower. SCP-5368 is remarkably aggressive and territorial. All non-personnel must not come in contact with it. If aggravated, SCP-5368 will become hostile and attempt to destroy anything in its vicinity. All SCP Foundation personnel guarding SCP-5368 must immediately respond and engage until SCP-5368 reverts back to its passive mode, which averagely lasts from 30 minutes to 2 hours. Air support is necessary as it will presumably bring the time of aggravation down by half an hour, but still remains harmless to SCP-5368. Any non-personnel who come into contact with SCP-5368 must be given amnestics and misinformed by MTF Gamma-5.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Addendum 1 - History:</strong></span> Originally thought to be neutralized in 1942, the SCP Foundation and the British Armed Forces worked together to eliminate SCP-5368 and reported their research in the file below.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Archived&nbsp;Documents</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Archived&nbsp;Documents</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5368</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Presumed Neutralized (until further notice)</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Information regarding SCP-5368's anomalous properties is to be contained by standard procedures. The British Armed Forces and Royal Air Force have consented to aid the Foundation in neutralizing SCP-5368.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5368-B is Tiger tank 132, a tank designed specifically to eliminate armored divisions. Numerous amounts of arbitrary activity are seen in combat:<br /> SCP-5368-A consumes only salty contents. If given anything with sugar in it, it will turn hostile and proceed to rampage for 30 minutes.<br /> The armor plating on SCP-5368-B is unearthly, literally flattening shells that attempt to penetrate its frontal armor.<br /> The 88&#160;mm mounted gun is capable of shooting three times the distance a 105&#160;mm Howitzer is capable of firing.<br /> The MG34 machine guns mounted on SCP-5368-B are capable of shooting 1800 rounds per minute, twice the average amount of ammunition a normal MG34 can.<br /> The average speed of SCP-5368-B seen by allies scout planes is approximately 50 kph.<br /> Soldiers and civilians alike who had seen it all said similar descriptions of ancient symbols marked on the hull and turret of SCP-5368.</p> <p>These were all listed from all physical observations made during Operation Battleaxe and the 2nd Cyrenaica Offensive. As of November 16, 1942, SCP-5368 was declared MIA.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Chronological Events:</strong></span><br /> In 1940, French Resistance 307 had discovered a top-secret Nazi Laboratory, titled Unzerbrechliche Festung, 20 miles southwest of █████, containing SCP-5368. When the SCP Foundation got word of this, SCP Council Member ███████, undercover as a French Intelligence officer, sent the resistance orders to send their most skilled agents to infiltrate and gather intel on the asset. After 216 days, the intel requested was with a note from the resistance, saying that Specimen Verdeckter is nearing its finishing trials along with research data from Dr. ████ Schwliden. After this, further communication with French Resistance 307 has ceased. We have assumed the Waffen SS has terminated the resistance group.</p> <div class="blockquote"> <p><em>Translated by Dr. █████ Schneider</em><br /> **Content: **<br /> Specimen A - Verdeckter<br /> In 1936, December 12th, a meteorite infused with Verdeckter crashed 20 miles south of █████████. We have cleansed the area and spread the disinformation of a pilot who crashed an experimental aircraft. Verdeckter seems to be an entity that can fuse itself with an object. Further testing and studying need to be conducted.</p> <p><strong>Log Entry #4</strong></p> <p>02,07,1940<br /> Scientist: ████ Schwliden<br /> It seems the asset has unique abilities and capabilities. However, it also appears to be sentient, so we may be able to find a way to enhance our weapons without it seizing control.<br /> HH</p> <p><strong>Log Entry #35</strong></p> <p>06,27,1940<br /> Scientist: ████ Schwliden<br /> We finally managed to pacify Verdeckter using several tons of phosphate gas. We are nearing its final phases. I believe this can defeat the British limeys down in Africa.<br /> HH</p> <p><strong>Log Entry #91</strong></p> <p>10,15,1940<br /> Scientist: ██████ Von Trippon<br /> Scientist ████ Schwilden was unfortunately killed in an accident by Verdeckter on October 13, 1941. Our belief in phosphate has failed miserably. We believed it could succumb Verdeckter for eight months. Our top scientist ████ Schwilden, along with six other scientists and 26 of our most fanatical troops, are now buried outside ███████. We hope some new mixtures that we have created, called #████, #███, #████, and Project Ursula could last much longer and more effectively. However, if all else should fail, we need to activate Protocol Beseitigung.<br /> HH</p> <p><strong>Log Entry #121</strong></p> <p>12,19,1940<br /> Scientist: ██████ Von Trippon<br /> We have finally finished it; Project Ursula was a huge success. The prime ingredient of Project Ursula was Flerovium. We have decided on a Tiger I H model to fuse with Verdeckter. Although we would like to select the crew member, Mein Fuhrer has already decided to put the best crew member in there. I will replace the radio operator to make sure Verdeckter stays pacified at all times. If not, we will need to proceed with Protocol Beseitigung. We must prevent Verdeckter from falling into Allies hands at all costs.<br /> Sieg Heil, and HH</p> <p><strong>Contact:</strong><br /> <strong>1941-06-15 - 1941-06-17:</strong> British military officers first saw SCP-5368 during Operation Battleaxe. The British 8th Armored Divisions suffered heavy losses as they approached SCP-5368. British government officials, including General Montgomery, contacted the Foundation, requesting support in suppressing and neutralizing it. MTF ███████ was sent to assist. They were able to severely damage it before being overwhelmed by German artillery and air support, allowing SCP-5368 to escape. The Foundation has declared MTF █████████ deceased as 90% of their forces were wiped out in the process, and the remaining survivors were later KIA while defending against SCP-5368.</p> <p><strong>1942-01-29:</strong> During the Second Cyrenaica offensive, British scout planes rediscovered SCP-5368. Without MTF ███████, British defenses were quickly overwhelmed. MTF Gamma-5 and Epsilon-6 are currently crossing the mediterranean sea along with British Naval forces.</p> <p><strong>1942-02-27:</strong> Both MTF teams reached Cairo. The entire British front has collapsed. MTF Alpha-1 is currently on hold if MTF Gamma-5 and Epsilon-6 fail their mission. If they do, MTF Alpha-1 must be rushed into Jerusalem. The middle east and its oil supplies are crucial for our operations and assets stationed there.</p> <p><strong>1942-06-30:</strong> The entire German offensive has ground to a halt outside of El-Alamein. MTF Gamma-5 and Epsilon-6 discovered SCP-5368 is quite vulnerable to air attacks. Assistance from MTF-Omega 15 may be required if the RAF is unable to handle SCP-5368.</p> <p><strong>1942-08-26:</strong> SCP-5368 spearheaded an assault on El Alamein. MTF Gamma-5 was able to hold SCP-5368 off with local RAF air support. ███████ rockets may be used by the RAF to neutralize SCP-5368.</p> <p><strong>1942-09-08:</strong> SCP-5368 has been potentially neutralized. All MTF personnel is pulling out while MTF Epsilon-11 stays to omit any information of SCP-568 and MTF Gamma-5 searches for SCP-5368. All German forces are in full retreat.</p> <p><strong>1942-11-16:</strong> SCP-5368’s crew members surrendered to us along with Dr. ██████ Von Trippon. Although they would not give up SCP-5368’s location, Dr. ██████ Von Trippon interview sheds some more light on SCP-5368. In the meantime, SCP-5368 is to be declared MIA as MTF Gamma-5 is unable to locate the asset.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Interview</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;Interview</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>SCP-Foundation Interrogator █████████ Charles Interviews Dr. ██████ Von Trippon: 1943-01-05, 1323</strong></span></p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> Dr. ██████ Von Trippon’s interview after his capture did shed some light on SCP-5368 and other testings done at Site Unzerbrechliche Festung.<br /> <em>Translated by Dr. Schween</em></p> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Hello Dr. ██████ Von Trippon.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> Who are you?<br /> █████████ Charles: We are the SCP Foundation, which stands for Secure, Contain, and Protect. Be glad Allied forces did not capture you. You would have been through… <em>█████████ Charles rubs his chin</em> …some mild interrogations.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> <em>Pushes his glasses up</em> Is this not one?<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Oh, no. This conversation is an interview. We are here to give you an opportunity.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> What opportunity?<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> You may join our group so long as you maintain our secrecy and help us with our research. If not, we will turn you over the British MPs.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> I prefer to take my chances with you.<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Good. Now, tell us everything about Site Unzerbrechliche Festung.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> Unzerbrechliche Festung was only the first of many. Others are continuing the work we started.<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> <em>Raises an eyebrow</em> First of many? Describe the others.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> I do not know how many facilities, but I know there are many others. Verdeckter was only the beginning. We were experimenting with similar entities on Tiger tank 212 and 217 as well as fighter jets Me-262s for our aces.<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> I will pass this information onto my superiors.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> And they are?<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> I’m sorry. Even I do not get the privilege of knowing their names.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> Makes sense. Even we do not know the OberUndeckGesellschaft names.<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Wait. Who? <strong>What?!?</strong><br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> They are a Nazi secret organization that controls the most secretive WonderWaffe program. They are the mastermind behind all of our technology. Only Hitler ever talks to them. They experiment on things that could change all of humanity possibly. Anyone who is suspected of treason or deserting will be shot or assassinated. With that, will you grant me asylum as well if I work with you?<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Most definitely. You are one of the most valuable assets to us.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> Thank you.<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> No problem. I have to go now.<br /> <strong>Dr. ██████ Von Trippon:</strong> Will we talk again?<br /> <strong>█████████ Charles:</strong> Maybe.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Log ends, 1341&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> As a valuable asset to the Foundation, Dr. ██████ Von Trippon must receive asylum. All resources must be poured into this OberUndeckGesellschaft group. They could be a potential enemy against the Foundation. Further investigation into these other entities must be done as well. We must also investigate if they are cooperating with the Obskuracorps and worked with them on SCP-4217 previously.</p> </div> <p><strong>Addendum 2 - First Encounter Since 1942:</strong> In 1973, during the Yom Kippur War, an armored Egyptian tank division discovered SCP-5368&#160;200 miles southwest Cairo, Egypt. The transcript below is from a radio transmission between tank commanders ███████, code-named Charlie, and ████████████, code-named Golfer, who appear to be good friends.</p> <p>[[collapsible show=&quot;+ Open Transcript&quot; hide=&quot;- Close Transcript&quot;]]<br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> Hey [REDACTED]! I see an abandoned tank.<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong> Command, could this be the rogue Israeli tank platoon we’ve been looking for?<br /> <strong>Command:</strong> We couldn’t confirm if they were Israeli tanks or not. What is the tank’s description?<br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> It looks like an abandoned German Panzer from WWII.<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong> Command, permission to send two people to investigate?<br /> <strong>Command:</strong> Granted.<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong> [REDACTED] and [REDACTED], go check it out.<br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> Huh. I never knew there was a WWII tank battle here.<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong> There never was. So then how is it here?<br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> Uhh. [REDACTED]? Why is the tank starting to glow?<br /> <em>An ear-piercing shriek can be heard over the radio</em><br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> WHAT THE HE-<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong>[REDACTED] and [REDACTED], PULL BA-!<br /> <em>Two men are heard screaming as the sounds of a machine gun fills the air</em><br /> <strong>Command:</strong> What is goi-<br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> HOLY S<strong>*! OPEN FIRE! OPEN FIRE!<br /></strong>Command:** [REDACTED] and [REDACTED], hold your fire. I repeat, ho-<br /> <em>Eight T-54 guns are heard firing</em><br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> HOW CAN A WWII RELIC STOP A 100 MM RIFLED GUN???<br /> <strong>Charlie:</strong> This is [REDACTED], we are requesting a code red air support. I repeat, a c-<br /> <em>Eruptions and an unhuman like groaning noise was heard in the background</em><br /> <strong>Golfer:</strong> F***! ANYONE! PLEASE HE-<br /> *Transmission abruptly ends*</p> <p><em>SCP-Foundation forces rushed to the location where the incident happened, but SCP-5368 was unable to be identified. About ten years after this encounter, SCP-5368 was sighted on July 13, 1987, with the loss of a UN supply convoy heading to relieve “A” Company of the 35th Battalion (UN Service) of the Irish Army holding out against Katangese rebels during the Siege of Jadotville. SCP Foundation forces were able to chase SCP-5368 towards the now designated Site-318.</em></p> </div> </div> </div> <p><em>Further documentation is needed. Right now, a Russian tip suggests to us a top-secret stache of German documents with more information possibly located near Minsk. Foundation personnel is attempting to access this information currently. New missile technology in the ████████ sector must be finished quickly in case SCP-5368 breaches containment. We must also prevent the GOC from eliminating SCP-5368. If they attempt to, SCP-5368 may become more aggressive and perhaps move north, endangering western Europe.</em></p> <p>[[div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;]]<br /></p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5367">SCP-5367</a> | SCP-5368 | <a class="newpage" href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5369">SCP-5369</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djgamer5863" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6987246&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606767350" alt="DJGamer5863" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6987246)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djgamer5863" >DJGamer5863</a></span></p> 
