&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Interview&amp;nbsp;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE FOLLOWING LOG IS LEVEL 05 ACCESS ONLY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MEMETIC KILL AGENT IMPLEMENTED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewed:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5144-2| AKA: Amidias&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewer:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. Paul Blart | Level 4 Researcher&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword:&lt;/strong&gt; After failing to understand what caused the containment breach of 5144-1 and its reaction in the interview (See 5144-1 interview 4), 5144-2 was questioned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;Begin Log, October 31th, 20██ at 2:53 PM&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Hello SCP-5144-2. We have some questions about 5144-1&#039;s containment breach.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Continue.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;SCP-5144-1 seems very sensitive to the topic of his past, as well as SCP-1762. Do you know why?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Fuck. I knew it would catch up to us eventually.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;What?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Paul&amp;#8230; are you married?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Uh, yes.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Would you do anything for them?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Yes I would. I love them.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I see. Well, let me explain how this all started. Over ten thousand years ago, me and Mozart were jumping through universes. We found this one universe where humanity had traveled to the stars and grown an empire. They were at war with other races, as human nature makes them. Me and Mozart were weapons smugglers. I thought it was dangerous but he thought it would be &amp;quot;fun.&amp;quot; Damn idiot didn&#039;t have to fear death like I did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So yea, we were smuggling weapons through enemy territory to the humans. We had gotten quite a reputation and everyone in the universe knew of us. One day, we were heading through some enemy space to meet up with our weapons dealer. We got ambushed on a heavily forested planet by the Wings of Freedom. They were a group heavily intent on stopping humans from spreading out into the stars. Like a rebellion of sorts.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;So how much had humanity taken over?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;They had grown to a population of over three trillion and spread far past the andromeda galaxy. I don&#039;t remember the exact area of space they controlled.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Interesting&amp;#8230; Continue.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;So me and Mozart were captured by the rebellion by choice. I told the idiot that we should have just blasted our way out but he insisted that we stay and see what happens. They tossed us into an interrogation room and left us there for a few rotations. Some armed guards, not humans, came into the room on day 3 to ask us some questions. Turned out that the rebellion wanted us to work for them, to help them fight the humans. Me and Mozart talked it out and agreed to fight for them. However I soon learned why Mozart wanted to stay, damn idiot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Turns out he was quite&amp;#8230; interested&amp;#8230; in this one lifeform, the same lifeform who led the raiding party and caught us both. She was a pink ,humanoid dragon who went under the name of Sasha. I forgot to tell you, the Wings of Freedom were mostly all humanoid dragons, hence the name. That&#039;s like the plainest description I can give you, a humanoid dragon-like entity. (&lt;em&gt;a laugh&lt;/em&gt;) Anyways, yea he kind of fell in love with her.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Love at first sight?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Hah, yep. So&amp;#8230; first mission, raid and blow up a human weapons depot. The same one me and Mozart had been smuggling weapons from, so we knew the layout well. A group of 16 soldiers were dropped down. Led by Sasha, our commander, we just simply ran inside the building and started shooting at the humans. I&#039;m guessing that Mozart didn&#039;t tell the commander about his uh&amp;#8230; extreme usefulness in the heat of battle, because he either vaporized or trapped the humans inside in like five minutes. What we didn&#039;t expect was the reinforcements, some human had called for backup I guess.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After the rebellion had taken most of the weapons back to the ship, a drop ship landed on the far side of the factory. At least thirty human soldiers, armed to the teeth, stormed the facility. We lost three of the group before we realized what had happened. Mozart and the commander had been cut off from the rest of the group. The rest of the group, including me, fell back to the ship and waited for the commander and Mozart. Give it a few minutes, and Mozart came barreling out of the factory wall, with Sasha on his back. They got on the ship and we took off. I&#039;m guessing that the lovestruck idiot got the commander to notice him, perhaps&amp;#8230; They started going on more missions together, as well as engaging in more activities together. (&lt;em&gt;a chuckle&lt;/em&gt;) Mozart never used a gun before and had to learn the hard way how you have to compensate for the force launched back at you. Sasha taught him how to use a gun, make a makeshift explosive, and other weapons. Mozart shared with Sasha the stories of me and him traveling the cosmos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the next six years, him and Sasha were practically everywhere together. Including many nights where I would leave them in their quarters to&amp;#8230; have fun&amp;#8230; You know what I mean.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Ah I understand.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Yea. It was kind of living the dream for them. Well, until that day&amp;#8230;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*5144-2 started staring at the floor*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Amidias, you there?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Yes sorry. That day&amp;#8230; the day it all went to shit. One final mission it was thought, one final mission to deal enough damage to the human race. The point of this mission was to obtain a data chip with information that&amp;#8230; goddamnit I sound like I&#039;m parodying Star Wars ain&#039;t I?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Yes it sounds like it a bit.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Well, I am not joking around with this. Anyway, the mission was to collect a data chip with information on the human goal, to spread to the farthest reaches of the universe. As well as the proof of what they do to planets when they leave them. The point was to get the data and send it out to every race to let them know what humanity was doing, and hopefully turn everybody on the humans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An attack squad of five ships of twenty soldiers each. Led by Sasha and her right hand lieutenant, Mozart. The ships landed in a hangar of the facility that housed the data and immediately were met with resistance from the humans. Speed up some futuristic firefight and a lot of damage to my audio sensors, we got into the facility, grabbed the data chip, and were on our way out. Four of the ships had made it out, leaving me waiting for the commander&#039;s group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only Sasha and Mozart, in their group, survived. I saw them running toward the ship with Sasha carrying the data. They had almost reached it when&amp;#8230;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Amidias you there dude? If it&#039;s too much I can wait till later to get the rest.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;No. No, I can&#039;t keep it a secret any longer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They had almost reached the ship when Sasha was hit square in the back by a bullet. I heard her cry out in pain and looked outside the ship to see what had happened. Mozart held Sasha in his arms in the middle of the hangar. I barely heard her say to him &amp;quot;Thank you for this life.&amp;quot; before she gave him a kiss, then went limp. I scanned her body and&amp;#8230; she had died. The bullet had severed her spinal cord.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Then for the next few minutes, Mozart sat there crying with Sasha&#039;s body in his arms. Armed human guards soon circled him and warned him to surrender or they would shoot. Then, he stood up and said five words. &amp;quot;You did this to her.&amp;quot; The energy orb in his chest started to glow a dark red as well as his eyes. A wreath of red fire covered his body. The ground started to shake and dust began swirling around his feet, then all the guards started screaming in pain before turning to dust. But&amp;#8230; it didn&#039;t stop there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;He opened a portal and walked through it. To where specifically it went, I do not know. But I soon learned what he did.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Continue?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Genocide. Genocide on a cosmic scale. Whatever was controlling him, it raised his hand to the roof of the building, and in his fiery rage, he fired a massive burst of energy into the night sky. Then&amp;#8230; the end.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;What do you mean the end?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;It was like a chain reaction, that burst of light fired off into the sky and started igniting every single star, planet, and black hole. An insane person would compare it to connecting dots in the sky, but the dots don&#039;t explode with the force of a fucking supernova.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Dr. Blart is now sitting on the edge of their chair*&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;For 44 seconds, that&#039;s how long it took. 44 seconds for the chain reaction to swallow every single planet, star, and black hole in the cosmos. There was nothing left&amp;#8230; nothing. I and whatever was controlling Mozart, we were the last 2 living beings in that universe. Just a black void that was once a beautiful night sky. Just a void.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Then he stopped, the fire around him had died, he kneeled in front of Sasha&#039;s body, stopped glowing red, and passed out. Probably from the energy he emitted. (&lt;em&gt;sigh&lt;/em&gt;) I moved Sasha&#039;s body outside and gave her a burial. Then dragged Mozart into the ship. I tried to undo what had happened. I knew I couldn&#039;t wipe his memory, so I just suppressed some of it. I used a makeshift neural link to digitally enter his mind and alter it. I suppressed his memory of Sasha&#039;s death. Above it, I added fake memories of them succeeding in the mission and stopping the spread of humanity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When he awoke, three months later, I had set up a fake story. That the rebellion succeeded in stopping the humans. I made fake messages from Sasha to Mozart that they had left this universe to go to another one. There was a massive gap in his memory, and I convinced him that he just got drunk at a bar last night. He somehow bought it, and we left that barren universe on the fake quest to find Sasha.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Oh&amp;#8230; Jesus Christ. But that doesn&#039;t fully explain why he broke containment.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I believe that, the 1762 records subconsciously brought back the memory of Sasha&#039;s death, just for a second.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;That makes more sense.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Paul, you guys here at the Foundation handle some scary things. Things that could end the world with the snap of their fingers. But this, this is something different. I don&#039;t know what it is&amp;#8230; One thing is clear, Mozart &lt;em&gt;cannot&lt;/em&gt; remember Sasha&#039;s death! Do you understand?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Yes I do.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;sigh&lt;/em&gt; &amp;quot;I&amp;#8230; I fear I&#039;ve only made things worse.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Huh?&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I mean, what if I never suppressed his memories? Maybe he would have gotten over her dea-&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Amidias, I think you did the right thing.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;But&amp;#8230; what if all that anger is growing inside him? What if he breaks again? Paul, Mozart must &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;never&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; remember Sasha&#039;s death! If he does, he&amp;#8230; he will make an XK class End of the World scenario look like a fucking tea party!&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paul:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;I understand.&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5144-2:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;The worst part, he was going to propose to her after the mission. He told me that he was going to propose to her after they made it back to the safety of the rebellion. Why&amp;#8230; why did that bullet have to land!&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;End Log&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5144-1 has shown the same immense power like it did during the containment breach once before. It seems that 5144-1 underwent great mental trauma in the past and the trauma was suppressed by technology that SCP-5144-2 used.&lt;/p&gt;
