&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5144-5&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AKA:&lt;/strong&gt; The Fallen Fantasy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; No unauthorized personnel are allowed to enter SCP-5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5144-5 is an unknown reality or world connected to ours by SCP-5144-4, which was created by SCP-5144-1. 5144-5 is the landscape outside of the 5144-4 structure on that side. Access to 5144-5 is only accessible via a drilled tunnel from exit of 5144-4 to the surface. SCP-5144-5 seems to have one star it orbits, and 2 moons that orbit it. Time functions similar in 5144-5 as it does on earth. The day/night cycle seems consistent with Earth&#039;s.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The explored part of 5144-5 was once habited by seemingly intelligent lifeforms. The surrounding 5-7 kilometers from the shaft exit resembles a desert. Outside of that is a forest, not resembling any flora on earth, that looks to have recently survived a forest fire. In the distance, a large mountain range is visible with 30% of it being held aloft by anomalous means.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5144-5 is mostly void of life in the explored sector. However, large wormlike entities are visible burrowing under the sand. Entities flee when loud noises above 150 decibels are emitted. Entities have armored plating that requires explosives to break through. No other living entities are documented in the explored sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anomalous Properties:&lt;/strong&gt; It is an alternate reality with unknown threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exploration Logs of 5144-5:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Explore the surface of SCP-5144-5&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparations:&lt;/strong&gt; Mining attempts on the other side of SCP-5144-4 recently broke through to the surface. D-20317, a male in his late 30s charged with homicide, was sent to the surface. D-20317 was given 1 days worth of food and water, a 9 millimeter pistol, a compass, a military knife, a head mounted camera, and a field kit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Researcher Linda Brooke was put in-charge of the exploration of SCP-5144-5. 5144-2 has requested to observe the exploration alongside Ms. Brooke. The request was accepted. Ms. Brooke, SCP-5144-2, and 2 armed MTF made camp inside SCP-5144-4. Due to SCP-5144-5&#039;s anomalous time altering abilities, the camp had to be constructed on the opposite side of the Archway to that of Earth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Log:&lt;/strong&gt; D-20317 was deployed at exit point of the mining shaft. Class-D said they noticed a desert-like landscape surrounding them. D-20317 took samples of the sand, remarking that there were many white chips in the sand. Class-D said that there are large boulder-like rock formations spread around the landscape, as well as dead trees scattered around. Video footage shows the trees not resembling any flora native to Earth. D-20317 turns the camera to the sky to view a sun with a yellow-ish orange hue. Class-D was instructed to pull out compass, of which they did. The compass did not function properly, instead spinning around rapidly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Linda Brooke asked the Class-D, via radio, if they noticed any structures nearby. D-20317 claims to see some large floating mountains in the distance. The video footage showed a mountain range with at least 30% of the mountains suspended in the air by unknown means. D-20317 was instructed to attempt to climb one of the large sandstone boulders to get a better vantage point. Class-D began running toward the closest boulder when they claimed to have felt a shaking in the ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5144-2 noticed something in the video feed, a large mound of sand moving at high speed toward the D-class. D-20317 was instructed to return to the mining shaft. Class-D began sprinting to the shaft but tripped on a large white rock protruding from the sand. The video camera was dislodged from the helmet on D-20317 when they tripped and fell. The footage shows Class-D firing off 3 shots with the 9mm at the mound of sand. A large wormlike entity burst out of the sand and consumed the D-class before burrowing back into the ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Explore surface of SCP-5144-5. Reclaim supplies and samples carried by D-20317.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secondary Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Capture and study wormlike entity if possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparations:&lt;/strong&gt; Level 2 Scientists Anton and Mikkel Schmidt and MTF Cadet Rosaline Jenson were sent to the surface of SCP-5144-5. Anton was given a field kit, a liter of water, 7 energy bars, a knife, and a flashlight. Mikkel was given a head mounted camera, sample flasks, an emergency flare, and a 9 millimeter pistol. Rose was armed with a FN P90, a concussion grenade, 5 clips of ammunition, and a lighter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Log:&lt;/strong&gt; Anton and Mikkel arrived on time. Rosaline 5 minutes later. The group entered the mining shaft and began their ascent. Once reaching the surface, Cadet Rose says that it is currently nighttime on 5144-5. Camera footage shows 2 moons orbiting the planet. No familiar stars or constellations are visible. Mikkel obtained what was left of D-20317&#039;s supplies; the camera, field kit, and backpack. They placed the items inside the opening of the mining shaft. Anton examines the white rock D-20317 tripped over and finds a vaguely human skull. Skull is placed in field kit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MTF Cadet Rose claims to have felt a rumbling in the ground. Mikkel and Anton agree. After 26 seconds of rumblings, the wormlike entity attempted to burrow under Rosaline and consume them. The cadet jumped out of the way and avoided the attack. Rose and Mikkel begin firing upon the entity and cause it to begin fleeing. Scientist Anton grabbed the concussion grenade from the MTF&#039;s belt and threw it at the entity. The grenade explodes and the creature ceases movement. Rosaline unloads a clip of ammunition into the body to confirm termination. Anton proceeded to use his knife to cut open the entity&#039;s abdomen to extract samples of blood and tissue. The entity bleeds a yellow liquid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mikkel requests the group return to SCP-5144-4, but is denied. The team is instructed to gain a vantage point on top one of the large sandstone formations. Cadet Rosaline takes the video camera from Anton and begins scaling one of the larger boulders. Once reaching the top, Rose holds the camera in the air and slowly circles around. Camera footage catches the &amp;quot;floating&amp;quot; mountain range, a large white rock formation, and a burnt forest obscuring a structure. The group are instructed to return to SCP-5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Mission Data:&lt;/strong&gt; The samples of the sand show the white chips to be shards of glass. The discovered skull seems to be human in size, however having a larger brain case and more accentuated jaw. Tests on the wormlike entities&#039; blood and tissue do not give indication of any relation to lifeforms native to earth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Explore SCP-5144-5. Reach and infiltrate structure located inside forest about 3 kilometers from exit point of 5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secondary objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Locate intelligent life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparations:&lt;/strong&gt; MTF Lambda-5 (&amp;quot;White Rabbits&amp;quot;) are prepared for traveling across SCP-5144-5 toward a structure sighted inside a forest roughly2 kilometers from 5144-4. Researcher Linda Brooke and SCP-5144-2 will remain in radio contact with the MTF squad back at SCP-5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Log:&lt;/strong&gt; MTF Lambda-5 deployed at exit point of 5144-4 and began traversing across the desert-like landscape. The squad took 29 minutes of walking through the desert region before reaching the forest. Many of the MTF describe the forest as being &amp;quot;long dead&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;scorched&amp;quot;. The trees, in the video footage, are seemingly charred. Trees are about 2 to 2.5 meters wide. No leaves are present on the trees. The squadron also claims to see a low fog drifting across the forest floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MTF reach the structure 36 minutes after deployment. The structure seems to be not one, but many house shaped buildings constructed in the canopy of the trees. Lambda-5 located a wooden stairway near the base of one of the trees and began their ascent. When reaching the top, a path of boards connecting the buildings in the trees are all connected to the single stairway tree. Most of the paths are damaged and not crossable, however the group find one and follow it to the building it&#039;s connected to. Video footage shows the structure having wooden shingles on the roof, glass windows, and a large door 2.2 meters tall. The windows of the structure are shattered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MTF entered the building to find 2 chairs, a table, a large bed, and some crates in the corner. All the items inside the building are slightly large for a human to use. All items are also slightly burnt. Sitting in one of the chairs is a 6.5 foot tall skeleton, blackened from exposure to flame. Another skeleton, 6.7, was found on the floor near the bed. 2 digits from the hands of each skeleton were collected as samples. Video footage shows the skeleton skulls resembling the same skull found during SCP-5144-5 exploration mission 1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After inspection, the skeleton on the floor seems to have been holding a small box. The box was placed inside a field kit. Further inspection shows the crates in the corner to be filled with unknown foodstuffs, as well as fabric and possible items or weaponry. The objects are damaged by fire way too much to be confirmed. The squadron left the structure and returned to the forest floor. MTF Lambda-5 were instructed to return to SCP-5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Mission Data:&lt;/strong&gt; Examination of the small box shows the contents not to be damaged by fire. The contents were as follows. A small feather with an insertion at the tip, possible use as a pen. Dried black liquid, suggested to be ink. And a piece of paper with the following text on it. The text is surprisingly in English. Some of the message is damaged and unreadable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dear Family,&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Anahita and I will return to you soon. We are finishing our work&lt;/em&gt; [Damaged] &lt;em&gt;and will be back for the journey to the new land. Please prepare for the journey when we arrive, we cannot waste time. They are burying the room in a fort night. We will reach you before&lt;/em&gt; [Damaged]. &lt;em&gt;Good travels.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;love,&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
[Damaged]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The letter refers to the burying of a &amp;quot;room&amp;quot; and a family traveling to a &amp;quot;new land&amp;quot;. Sadly there is not enough information to understand what happened.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Set up temporary/ permanent base of operations on surface of SCP-5144-5.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Target Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Large white rock formation.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Estimated time:&lt;/strong&gt; 8 hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparations:&lt;/strong&gt; A group consisting of 3 scientists and 7 members of the MTF Lambda-5 unit were deployed at the surface of SCP-5144-5. Each member has 2 days worth of food and water, as well as a fold up tent and matches. All scientists are also given a field kit each to collect samples. Radio contact is kept between the exploration team and basecamp inside SCP-5144-4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Log:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Day 1-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The exploration team was deployed at the exit point of the mining shaft connecting SCP-5144-4 to the surface of 5144-5. The group began traversing the desert landscape in the direction of the large rock formation. 1 hour of traveling, the group encountered another wormlike entity like was encountered during the first and second exploration missions. Entity was terminated, no casualties reported.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The exploration team, about 3 hours into the journey, claim to have spotted a large flying object in the sky. Camera footage shows a large bird-like entity, estimated 9 meters tall, with red feathers, flying high above the group. The entity flew closer and landed on a sandstone boulder roughly 30 meters from the group. It began hitting the boulder it stood on with its large beak. The noise seems to have alerted one of the worm creatures, which began burrowing underground toward the boulder. The bird entity flew into the air and dove at the moving sand mound, spraying sand over the group. Camera footage was temporarily lost. After the team recovered, footage shows the bird entity back on the boulder consuming the worm. One of the MTF cadets made a joke about &amp;quot;the early bird getting the worm&amp;quot; which made some of the group laugh. Exploration team continued travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team reached the large white rock form in 4 hours and 34 minutes. The rock formation is actually a massive skeletal structure about 200 meters long. The form looks vaguely similar to a lizard skeleton, however distinct horns are found on the back of the skull. The skeletal structure is damaged, with breaks in the ribcage and spine visible. 2 unknown appendages, possibly secondary arms, are located near the midsection of the entity. Scientists Anton and Mikkel Schmidt took samples of the bone. The team locate the skull of the deceased organism and make camp inside the open jaw of it. The maw of the creature is forced open by a large boulder that has broken half of the jaw on the right side. Evidence suggests the entity fell on the boulder and shattered its jaw on impact, however was probably dead before impact. One of the MTF noticed the sun setting in 5144-5 and started a small fire inside the skull. The group were instructed to rest for the next day. 2 MTF cadets held watch at the front of the skull.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Day 2-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The group were awoken around 5:00 AM, in 5144-5, to the sound of thunder. Video footage showed a large storm coming toward the desert area from the &amp;quot;floating&amp;quot; mountain range. The storm itself seemed that of a thunderstorm. However when lightning would strike, a large &amp;quot;tornado&amp;quot;, as one scientist described it, of lightning would strike the ground for approximately 32 seconds. The group are warned to stay inside the skull of the deceased organism until the storm passes. Radio contact was lost for 6 hours when the storm got between the camp at 5144-4 and the team in the field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Day 3-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radio contact was restored. The storm had passed. The exploration group had begun rationing out food and water and were preparing to return to 5144-4. Level 3 Researcher, Linda Brooke, at 5144-4 gave them permission to return. The team returned to the exit shaft of 5144-4 in 3 hours and 59 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Mission Data:&lt;/strong&gt; Chemical analysis does not show any connection from the deceased organism to that of Earthly life. The next few weeks after the mission, an airlock was constructed at the exit point of the mining shaft. 2 more missions to the skeleton structure camp were sent with supplies to reinforce the camp and make it more suitable for long-term survival. These missions did not have any significance and the logs were discarded.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;+&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Exploration&amp;nbsp;log&amp;nbsp;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Objective:&lt;/strong&gt; Long term exploration mission.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Target Location:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;quot;Floating&amp;quot; Mountain range.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Estimated time:&lt;/strong&gt; Unknown.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preparations:&lt;/strong&gt; A group of 3 scientists, Anton and Mikkel Schmidt and Mary Williams, and 2 members of MTF unit Lamdba-5, Rosaline Jenson and Jim Williams, were sent from the skeleton basecamp in the direction of the mountain range. Each scientist was armed with a field kit, a military knife, a 9 millimeter pistol with 5 clips of ammo, a box of matches, and a fold up tent. Each MTF were armed with FM-P90s, 2 concussion grenades each, a military knife, 20 clips of P90 ammunition, a box of matches, and a fold up tent. Furthermore, the group were given 3 horses for travel. The group was also given 3 months worth of food and 4 weeks of water. Snow is visible on the mountains, so it suggests water will be there. Finally, the group was also given one video camera to log their findings if they are to return.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: line-through;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission Log:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This mission is currently ongoing. Radio contact was lost near the base of the mountain range. No recovery teams have been sent as of yet.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footer-wikiwalk-nav&quot;&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wolfmandeth&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6859403&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1606767351&quot; alt=&quot;Wolfmandeth&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6859403)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wolfmandeth&quot;  &gt;Wolfmandeth&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
