					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/774515350721134612/unknown.png" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="unknown.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>Artwork of First sighting SCP-5144 by Anne Bookevich</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> A Multiversal <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Joy</span>ride</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe | Euclid | Keter</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144 is <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">3</span> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">4</span> 5 separate entities/objects. 5144-2 and 5144-3 have been contained but 5144-1 cannot be contained by any means in this reality (See SCP-5144-1 log for details). SCP-5144-4 is a titanic marble structure located in Iceland that is a gateway to another reality. SCP-5144-5 is an alternate reality of which connected to ours by SCP-5144-4 (See 5144-4 and 5144-5 logs for more details).</p> <p>The containment cell of SCP-5144-1, 5144-2, and 5144-3, is a large aircraft hangar sized room located 30 meters underground at Site 38. The hangar is partially taken up by SCP-5144-3 due to its size. The entrance to the cell is a 10 by 6 foot sized metal door. Clustered near the entrance are some cushioned chairs and a coffee table. On the walls of the cell are paintings of other worlds and entities. Small statues are scattered around the room. A desk covered in pieces of metal is located near the sculptures, this is where SCP-5144-1 constructs them. The builds resemble miniature models of SCPs that have been used on 5144-1 in termination attempts.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| First Contact:</strong> Upon March 17th, 20██ at 1:19 PM, SCP-179 was seen pointing toward the planet Neptune. On the far side of the planet, light distortions were visible. The light distortions continued for 2 hours before a massive explosion came from it. The explosion resembled a small supernova, which vaporized about 40% of Neptune's upper atmosphere. Out of the explosion a comet was seen on a direct collision course with Earth. Within 5 minutes, the comet had made it from Neptune to the Moon and slowed drastically. While passing by Mars, a radio transmission was picked up coming from the comet.</p> <p><strong>Radio Transmission detected:</strong> &quot;Hallo! Hallo! Ist da jemand? Dies ist [DATA LOST] der [DATA LOST] Freiheit, die um Erlaubnis zur Landung bittet! Mein Schiff ist [DATA LOST] beschädigt und ich muss Reparaturen durchführen. Ist [DATA LOST] bewohnbar?! Ich wiederhole: Ist die Erde bewohnbar?!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Radio Transmission Translation:</strong> &quot;Hello! Hello! Is anyone there? This is the [DATA LOST] of the [DATA LOST] freedom, asking for permission to land! My ship is [DATA LOST] damaged and I need to repair it. Is [DATA LOST] habitable?! I repeat, is Earth habitable ?! &quot;</p> <p>Attempts to connect to the individual on the radio failed. The anomalous comet continued on its way to Earth, slowing gradually as it entered the atmosphere. At 3:28 the comet crashed in a field near Finley, Tennessee.</p> <p>A large meteorite is found by researchers sitting in a 10 feet deep crater with the diameter being around 70 meters. The nearby oak forest had been scorched by the crash as well as an abandoned farmhouse. No one seemingly was injured during the crash. The Foundation quickly set up a perimeter around the crater and kept any news media from getting near the meteorite.</p> <p>March 20th, 20██ at 6:57 PM, 3 days after the meteorite crashed. The meteorite began shaking for 30 seconds before it &quot;turned into water&quot; says one of the researchers who tested the liquid to make sure. Inside the crater now lay a mysterious metal machine surrounded by a puddle of water. Scientists attempted to get samples of the machine but failed, no tools or weapons the Foundation had on site could damage the construct.</p> <p>March 21st, 20██ at 12:34 PM, loud banging could be heard from inside the machine. D-class personnel was sent in to investigate the noises. The D-class claims to hear voices, yelling, inside the machine. Foundation agents told the D-class to try to make contact with the voice, of which the D-class did. The voice instructed them to locate a cargo bay door and remove and blockages.</p> <p>The D-class followed the voice to the back of the machine and was instructed by the voice to remove the dirt blocking a large cargo bay door. An armed guard brought the D-class a shovel and they proceeded to remove the dirt. After it was cleared, a loud banging came from inside the cargo bay. 2 minutes of banging went on before the cargo bay door blasted open, heaving the entire machine a few feet in the air. Out of the machine came 2 figures; human male in a tuxedo and a large, dark blue creature (SCP-5144-1 and SCP-5144-2.)</p> <hr /> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/778444314212171796/wolf_thinggy_idrk_1_half_hours_hhhhhhhhhhhhh.png" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="wolf_thinggy_idrk_1_half_hours_hhhhhhhhhhhhh.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>SCP-5144-1 digital artwork by Researcher Arthur Johnson</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> Mozart</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Euclid</span> Keter</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144-1 cannot be contained by the Foundation but the lifeform does stay inside 5144's containment cell at Site 38 by choice. The 5144-1 can't be contained because of one of its anomalous abilities (Seen below).</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5144-1 is a bipedal reptilian lifeform. Approximately 2.5 meters in height and weighs over 200kg. The flesh of the entity is a dark grey and the skin is covered by millions of small, dark blue scales. 5144-1 has a large head, in the shape of a snake head, with a pair of eyes on each side of the skull. Nostrils are located above the front lip. Entity has 4 fangs located inside its maw, 2 inches long each, that secrete the MF-1 substance in extremely concentrated amounts. The eyes glow light blue. The creature can communicate verbally despite a lack of vocal cords or tongue. The chest cavity of the creature is visible with a glowing blue orb floating inside it. The orb does not show up on any scanners however the hume level does. Inside the chest cavity of 5144-1, the hume level rapidly increases and decreases at an unsteady rate, however not affecting the hume level outside the chest cavity. If 5144-1 consumes any item, when the item enters the chest cavity, it is absorbed by the orb.</p> <p>The lifeform's skeletal structure is constructed entirely of an unknown metal. Attempts to study the metal have failed due to 5144-1's anomalous ability. Whatever the bones are made of seems to have the same density as steel. The creature has only 3 digits on its hands/feet. Upon 5144-1's back are 4 hatches, each 4 inches in diameter, that open to extend long robotic limbs of the same metal the skeleton is constructed from. The limbs can extend up to 2 meters in length and each have a robotic hand on them. The robotic hands have 4 digits each. The robotic limbs can retract back into the body of 5144-1 however there is no visible changes to the chest cavity of the entity. SCP-5144-1 has a large serpentine tail stretching 2.5 meters in length with large plates made of the same skeletal alloy fused to the top.</p> <p>Adorned on the tip of the tail is a small flower similar to a water lily, however glowing a pink hue. Inside the center of the flower is a cluster of powder known as MF-1 substance. The substance causes sedation if inhaled or consumed. When burned, MF-1 becomes an extremely powerful hallucinogen and sense dampener. SCP-5144-1 seems to be immune to the sedative ability but is still susceptible to the hallucinogen. SCP-5144-1 has its spine protected by smaller plates similar to the ones on its tail. Entity has no digestive organs. The respiratory system of the entity pumps a dark blue blood through the body of unknown means, as no lungs or heart are existent within 5144-1. SCP-5144-1 prefers to be identified as &quot;Mozart&quot;.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1's origins are unknown. SCP-5144-1's knowledge of its existence is limited.</p> <p><strong>Behavior:</strong> SCP-5144-1 is a rather benevolent lifeform. It is quite open to the Foundation of its existence however will not talk about a specific time in its past around 10 thousand years before contact. 5144-1 also seems to feel happy by making others feel happy, including trying to cheer up one guard who lost a friend in a containment breach at another site. The SCP seems to want to help the Foundation.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1 prefers creating things. It will generally will construct canvases then paint detailed images of places it's been to and lifeforms it's seen. It will then try to show staff the paintings and explain the worlds they are of. But when questioned about a painting of a pink reptilian humanoid, 5144-1 refuses to talk. The creature also seems to enjoy constructing metal sculptures of other SCPs, weapons of alien construct, and otherworldly furniture. SCP-5144-1 donates its alien weapons to the researchers to study and possibly distribute to MTF units.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1 has no sexual attraction to humans. However, it has shown interest in SCP-1472, claiming that Dr. Bright said something about Velociraptors in maid costumes. SCP-5144-1 has sent 4 requests to Dr. Paul Blart for permission to enter SCP-1472, permission has been denied.</p> <p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> SCP-5144-1 has proven not to be able to die. The central orb cannot be damaged by any known methods. The body of 5144-1 is durable but still destroyable. However when removed from the majority of the body or destroyed, the limbs or remaining body will disintegrate only to reconstruct around the central orb. If any portions are still missing after reconstruction, the nearest object will begin to disintegrate and reconstruct the missing body portions until the body is complete, then cease disintegration of nearest object.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1 can launch concentrated heat from the palms of its robotic limbs. The beams of heat exceed over 2000 degrees Celsius but the heat stays confined to the 4 inch diameter of the robotic limbs. When activated, four beams of blue light protrude from the central core of 5144-1 and proceed to move through the flesh to connect where the robotic limbs enter the body. It is suggested that the energy is drawn from the central orb, but this theory is not fully proven.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1 seems to have atom altering abilities. 5144-1 can manipulate the atomic makeup of any item and change it into something else. The manipulation seems to take a great amount of energy from 5144-1. The more complex something is, the harder it is for 5144-1 to change it. A simple glass cup is easier to alter than a motherboard of a computer. When exerting too much energy, 5144-1 will cease life functions, resulting in it falling to the ground, for approximately 25 to 30 seconds before restarting. 5144-1 afterwards will remain unconscious until it has regained its strength.</p> <p>SCP-5144-1 can open portals to other universes/realities. It does this by firing 4 separate heat beams at a single point. When all four beams connect, it opens a portal that gets larger the longer 5144-1 continues its bombardment. The portals close shortly after being opened. The entity seems not to be able to control the reality that a portal is opened to, however this is possibly not true (See 5144-1 containment breach).</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">|5144-1&nbsp;Containment&nbsp;Breach|</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">|5144-1&nbsp;Containment&nbsp;Breach|</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>SCP-5144-1 Breach</p> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Breach cause:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p> <p><strong>&lt;Breach&gt;</strong></p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">On August 26th, 20██ at 7:28 PM</span></p> <p><strong>Distress call:</strong> &quot;Emergency! This is Dr. Paul Blart. SCP-5144-1 just broke containment! I repeat, 5144-1 has broken containment! Site 38 requesting assistance!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Ok. Dispatching MTF unit Omega-7 to your location. The MTF unit will be there momentarily.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">8:23 PM</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;We have reached Site 38, no fatalities. SCP-5144-1 seems to have broken through the roof of its containment cell. SCP-5144-1 is currently sprinting at 60 miles per hour to an unknown location. We are in pursuit in helicopters with Dr. Paul Blart. SCP-5144-1 is also currently enveloped in a dark red flame!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Continue your pursuit! You have full authorization to attempt to slow 5144-1's movement. Terminate it if you need to.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Affirmative. *off mic* Omega-7, begin firing upon SCP-5144-1!&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">8:44</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Command, SCP-5144-1 is not slowing its speed. We can't do enough damage up here!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Understood. Attempt to deploy units in 5144-1's path!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Yes command. *off mic* Deploy MTF in helicopters 2, 3 and 5 in SCP-5144-1's path!&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">8:47</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Command! We have casualties!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;What happened?&quot;</p> <p>**Omega-7 Commander: &quot;SCP-5144-1 disintegrated helicopters 2, 3 and 5, along with all MTF inside them! Its pace has not slowed. SCP-5144-1 also fired an energy beam and took down helicopter 4, no casualties in 4.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Continue pursuit at safe distance!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> *off mic* &quot;Give me that!&quot; *on mic* &quot;MTF Command, is there anything in the direction it's currently heading?!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Site-██ is in its current direction. You are about 120 miles from it.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Inform all staff at that site to evacuate! SCP-5144-1 is going to barrel right through it like it did the helicopters!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;We will.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">10:45</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 is nearing Site-██ and starting to slow!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Evacuation is in progress. How long until it gets there?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 has stopped! It is currently standing outside the site gate. Wait no, it just disintegrated the gate! I repeat, 5144-1 just disintegrated the gate. It is entering the site.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Remain safe distance. We will warn personnel inside.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">10:51</span></p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;We are monitoring the site camera system. SCP-5144-1 has entered researcher Takenaka's office. Takenaka is currently trapped inside with it. SCP-5144-1 is standing across the desk from Takenaka.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">10:53</span></p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 just threw Takenaka into the wall and has taken SCP-1762! It is leaving the room.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">11:01</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Command! We have visual on SCP-5144-1! It has exited the site and is carrying SCP-1762 with a robotic limb coiled around it. The fire encasing 5144-1 is not damaging 1762. Do we engage?&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Negative. Remain safe distance but continue pursuing 5144-1.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Yes Comman-&quot; *loud explosion*</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Commander? Omega-7 do you copy?!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Commander:</strong> &quot;Command, helicopter 1 has been shot down. 2 casualties. Helicopters 6, 7, and 8 will continue pursuit.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Affirmative.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;Command, this is helicopter 6. SCP-5144-1 has broken into a sprint approximately 80 miles per hour and rapidly increasing!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Continue pursuit.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">1:36</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;Command. SCP-5144-1 has just reached the Atlantic ocean but shows no sign of stopping. It is freezing the water below it while it's running!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Maintain pursuit. You cannot lose SCP-5144-1.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">3:12</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;Command. SCP-5144-1 has just reached land. Current location is the southwestern side of Iceland. We are also running low on fuel for the helicopters.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Maintain pursuit until yo-&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 has stopped! I repeat, 5144-1 has stopped!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Land a safe distance from SCP-5144-1.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">4:19</span></p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 is currently in a kneeling position in front of SCP-1762, which is a few feet from it.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;Dr. Blart. Stay away from 5144-1.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;What is happening?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 just stood up!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Unknown voice:</strong> &quot;<em>YOU DON'T GET TO ABANDON HUMANITY!</em>&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;What what that!?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 just threw SCP-1762! 1762 got 70 meters or so before 5144-1 began firing energy beams at it!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;He&#8230; He's crossing the beams!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;What does that mean?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;He said that crossing the beams opens-&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> &quot;Command! A bright light is coming from SCP-1762's locatio- *a loud explosive noise* COMMAND! A giant beam of light is shooting into the sky where 1762 was!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;We are connecting to your body cams.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;The beam&#8230; its getting bigger! It just enveloped SCP-5144-1!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Get out of there!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Lieutenant:</strong> *off mic* &quot;Get those choppers in the air NOW!&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">4:29</span></p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Hello? Lieutenant?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;We barely made it out of there but the helicopters are practically out of fuel. Command&#8230; the beam shooting in the sky is now about 2 fucking kilometers large!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> *off mic* &quot;Guys look out the window&#8230;&quot; &quot;Jesus christ!&quot; *on mic* &quot;We have visual on the beam of light. Where is the lieutenant?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;The lieutenant is gone. He was absorbed by the beam of light. As well as helicopter 8. The beam has stopped growing in size and I can see movement inside it.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Are you a safe distance?!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Yes.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Ok. We are sending help.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">6:48</span></p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Command! There is some kind of structure inside the beam of light! I can see something in there. Something big. It just stopped! Command the beam of light is gone! Oh&#8230; oh my god!&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Blart? What is happening?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Holy shit! There is a titanic shape where the beam of light was! It&#8230; it looks to be made out of some sort of white material.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;How big is the structure?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Command. Its the fucking size of the beam! WAIT! Oh god where is 5144-1?!&quot; *the mic is heard dropping to the floor*</p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Cadet:</strong> &quot;C.. Command? Dr. Blart just ran off toward the structure. What should I do?&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Stay there. Help should be arriving shortly.&quot;</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">7:12</span></p> <p><strong>Omega-7 Cadet:</strong> &quot;Command. Dr. Blart is back. He dragged SCP-5144-1 behind him. Here he is.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;Command.&quot;</p> <p><strong>MTF Command:</strong> &quot;Blart what happened?! Why did you leave?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Dr. Paul Blart:</strong> &quot;I went to the structure and found 5144-1 passed out on the floor. The structure is massive. Get researchers out here now! We need to know what this thing is!&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;Breach Secured&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Interviews of SCP-5144-1:</strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5144-1| AKA: Mozart</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Arthur Johnson | Level 4 researcher</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> 5144-1 was questioned of its existence and reason for coming to Earth.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log, March 23rd, 20██ at 5:30 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP-5144-1. I hear you like being called Mozart, is that correct?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yes, that is correct.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Ok. Now we have wanted to know, Why did you come here? To this planet I mean.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Alright big backstory time with Mozart. So a few&#8230; what about 30,000 years ago? Sorry I stopped counting after 700. I just woke up I guess? I don't remember anything before then, just waking up and started existing.</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Ok. *Arthur wrote down the date in his notebook* Now please continue.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I woke up in the void I guess? No stars, no noise, just nothingness. In my hand I clutched a tiny metal disk. After a few minutes of understanding what it felt like to move limbs, I fumbled with the disk and a little hologram turned on.</p> <p>A tiny figure stood on the disk. He had one eye and some funny horns, as well as a slightly uh&#8230; large body. Actually I can show you the hologram. *SCP-5144-1 placed the disk on the table and turned it on*</p> <p>(See Hologram Message)</p> <p>I was so confused after watching that but after a few months floating in space with the ability to not die, I learned how to harness my abilities. Somehow I knew already how to speak and how to use my abilities. I gotta say though, it was a weird experience. Anyways, I learned how to open portals and entered a new universe.</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> *Arthur was staring at 5144-1 before snapping out of it* &quot;Wow&#8230; that must have been a very odd experience. How did you specifically get to our universe though?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh right! Me and Amidias are on a conquest across the cosmos. Like a multiversal joyride. We uh&#8230; ran into some trouble. I was kinda was in the middle of a military space battle. Bullets and missiles flying everywhere. I just got stuck in the middle of it when it started and had to open a rift to get out of there. However, my ship was hit by a rogue missile and that's why it looked like a ball of fire coming down here.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Jeez, that is something else. Why was there fighting?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Some alien lifeforms having a weird dispute over space and territory I think.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Wow. Thanks Mozart, this has been quite an enlightening interview.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;No problem dude. See ya later.&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log, March 23rd, 20██ at 5:40 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-1 is an interdimensional traveler that does not know how it even exists.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5144-1| AKA: Mozart</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Linda Brooke | Level 3 Researcher</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was interviewed before a test of its atom restructuring abilities.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log, April 2nd, 20██ at 10:45 AM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP-5144-1, my name is Linda. We have some questions for you then we want to test your anomalous abilities. Is that ok?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Sure doc, ask away.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;We have some questions about SCP-5144-3, your ship. What is it constructed of?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Er&#8230; Don't remember. I bought it from some guy in the Messier 82 galaxy.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Interesting. *Linda writes on her notepad* Ok now there were some odd items inside your ship. Starting with the cargo bay, what was in there?&quot;</p> <p><strong>SCP-5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh yea! The fruit crates in there I picked up on an uncharted planet a few lightyears from where Earth should have been. I didn't check though. There should have also been my fancy knife somewhere in there&#8230; I think that's everything in the cargo bay.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> *Finishes writing notes down* &quot;Ok now there were also some lockers in the top level of 5144-3 containing many different items. Can you explain what they are and why you have some of them?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;There's some canned meat and water in there. &quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Lets see, there's the laser rifle I got in there&#8230; <em>Oh God not the grenades!</em>&quot;</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Calm down. 5144-2 left you a note in the locker to remind you what they were. We did not touch them.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 sat back down in his seat*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Phew. Ok I think the last thing is a mirror? I don't remember where I got it.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Wait, we found something else in one of the lockers. A photo album with pictures you and another lifeform waving at the camera. Can you tell us what this is?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I&#8230;I really rather not talk about it&#8230;&quot;</p> <p>*a tear drips down 5144-1's cheek.*</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Ok, I see it is a hard topic for you. Let's move onto the experiment. Please follow me.&quot;</p> <p>*Linda led SCP-5144-1 into an empty room with a coffee table and a pile of dirt on it.*</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Alright. We want to test your atom altering abilities. Can you please turn the pile of dirt into anything that comes to mind.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;<em>Anything?</em> Ok then, I got an idea.&quot;</p> <p>*Linda proceeded to back away as 5144-1's mechanical arms and palms started to glow. Then 5144-1 raised his right hand to aim at the pile of dirt and the dirt started to float slowly, particle by particle, into the air. 5144-1 then blasted the floating dirt with 1 beam of light from its arm, completely obliterating the floating mass.</p> <p>5144-1 then proceeded to raise all 4 mechanical arms on its back to face the same way his arm was aimed. Then the palm of his hand as well as the centers of the 4 robotic arms started emitting blue waves of light visible in the air. The waves crossed the room toward the area where the pile of dirt had been floating. Quickly the air around the location of where the dirt was started to distort as a tiny construct was becoming visible. The atoms had been in the air around the room and now were rejoining into something else. 2 minutes went by before 5144-1 was complete.</p> <p>After 5144-1 stopped emitting blue light waves, a gold microwave lay atop the coffee table. 5144-1 immediately passed out on the floor after the microwave was complete. The process seems to take an immense amount of energy from 5144-1.*</p> <p><strong>Linda:</strong> &quot;Get a stroller, move him back to his containment cell and&#8230;. Uh, move the microwave there too.&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log, April 2nd, 20██ at 11:02 AM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-1 can manipulate atoms of any item but requires a great amount of energy. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">A golden microwave is currently the most complex item it has created while in foundation custody.</span></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5144-1| AKA: Mozart</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Arthur Johnson | Level 4 Researcher</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> After waking from his comatose state, 5144-1 was interviewed about the incident.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log, October 30th, 20██ at 4:33 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Hello Mozart. How are you feeling?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Ugh&#8230; I feel kind of drained. What happened?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Actually, we were hoping you would know. Why did you breach containment?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;What!? Um, I don't know what you're talking about.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;You disintegrated the ceiling and ran off toward Site ██, then took an item from there and made your way to-&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Wait what? Dude, I was here.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Look up.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 looked to the roof and saw the 6 meter wide hole it made.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh dear. This isn't some joke. But wait, how did I do that? I should have dropped right outside the hole from the energy use&#8230;&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Yes we thought the same thing but you surprised us all.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh no! I didn't hurt anybody did I?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;You disintegrated an entire MTF squad&#8230;&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh god.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Mozart, what do you remember.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I was sitting on the couch reading some SCP articles on an iPad. Wait, there was something else. Right before I&#8230;&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;We looked at the iPad after we got you back here. You were reading an article about SCP-1762.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;What one was that? Some sort of bo- Box, a box&#8230; why does that seem so familiar.&quot; *5144-1 got up and started pacing around before gasping loudly* &quot;<em>I remember!</em>&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;You remember what?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;The box, the box of dragons. It&#8230; it's coming back to me. The article made me feel s&#8230; sad? Yea, I kinda wished I could have done something. But what?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Do you have memory problems frequently?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;No very rarely&#8230; A weird dream&#8230; <em>why</em> does something not seem righ-&quot; *5144-1 stopped abruptly and then muttered something unintelligible* &quot;I&#8230; I'm sorry Arthur I need to go.&quot; *5144-1 then ran toward 5144-3 and boarded it, closing the cargo bay behind it.*</p> <p><strong>Arthur:</strong> &quot;Mozart wait! We are in the middle of an interview.&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log, October 30th, 20██ at 4:37 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> Some data about the breach was uncovered but not enough to find out why 5144-1 breached containment.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hologram&nbsp;Recording</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hologram&nbsp;Recording</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>The following message was translated by SCP-5144-1.<br /> The message is in an unknown language.<br /> The metal disk that dispenses the hologram message has great wear and barely functions.</strong></p> <p><strong>&lt;Beginning Message Translation&gt;</strong></p> <p>Unknown Figure:</p> <p>It's been a long time Brother.<br /> I am sad you had to destroy yourself for those pitiful lifeforms below you. But you always were so fascinated by them. <em>*a chuckle*</em> You were always the one to look on the bright side of this painful existence. I remember when you turned the star ways I tore apart into beautiful tapestries of chaos. I do miss seeing them.</p> <p>*a pause*</p> <p>That world&#8230; You put so much time and love into that world. But why did you have to go destroy yourself for it? Was it worth it? All that pain?</p> <p>*another pause*</p> <p>My children have failed me. You are my last hope.<br /> I am imprisoned below the sand, and the child of light stands in the way of my freedom. If you are going to free me, you must destroy the child of light.<br /> Free me, Brother.<br /> So that I may destroy this painful existence, and you can create it a new from the ashes.<br /> Free me, Brother.</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Message Translation&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p><strong>Cross-Tests:</strong><br /> <strong>These are the logs of 3 cross-tests that all shared the similar feeling of Deja Vu from SCP-5144-1. No connection with the SCPs used for testing are found as of yet.</strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-3000</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-3000</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p> <p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-3000</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> To test 5144-1's immunity to cognitohazards, it was supposed to be introduced to the Y909 compound. However, 5144-1 insisted it go meet SCP-3000 face to face. The request was met with hesitation from head researchers but was accepted.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Test&gt;</strong></p> <p>*SCP-5144-1 exits the SCPF Eremita. It was given a waterproof radio it carried in one robotic hand, as well as a glass flask in its right hand. 5144-1 was instructed to expose itself to the Y909 compound and attempt to collect some of the compound in the flask.*</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;You are nearing SCP-3000. About 400 meters. Do you see anything?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Nope. Damn its pitch black out here. What am I looking for again?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;SCP-3000 resembles a massive serpent or eel-like lifeform.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;A big snake. Got it.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 is now 200 meters from 3000*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I gotta say, it's nice being able to float around like I'm in space. No stars, just blackness&#8230; *sigh* peaceful.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Please remain on task.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yea yea I know.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 is now 120 meters from 3000*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Uhh I think I found it.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1's tail flower casts a purple light across the face of SCP-3000. 3000 has started excreting the Y909 compound.*</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Please swim toward the Y909 substance.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;You mean the dark liquid right&#8230; Ugh! Why did I sign up for this.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 swam into the dark mass*</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Do you feel anything?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Not rea- *5144-1 started gagging* Disgusting! The compound tastes like spoiled milk.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Do you remember your task?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yep. Expose myself to some of the substance and then get a sample. I don't think I am forgetting anything.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Movement to your left! What do you see?&quot;</p> <p>*SCP-3000 had moved and was now looking at 5144-1*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;A large mouth and a ton of teeth. Uh&#8230; Hello ma'am?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Who are you speaking to?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Who do ya think&#8230; The snake. Woah that's weird.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;What is?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;This feels familiar, not the place but like, her. Like some weird Deja Vu. Maybe it's the Y909 stuff.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Be careful. We don't know what will happen if you are consumed.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Yea I know. She's kinda cute. Hah, she's smiling at me.&quot;</p> <p>*3000 had opened its mouth*</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Mozart get out of the way!&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 barely swam out of the way. 2 robotic limbs had been ripped off and consumed by 3000.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Woah there!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Retrieve the Y909 substance and return.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;On it.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 swam near the back of 3000's head and filled the flask it carried with the compound.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Aight, got the compound. Heading back to the sub.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;5144-1 incoming!&quot;</p> <p>*3000 lunged at 5144-1 again, this time biting off his tail*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;<em>Jesus woman</em>! I'm like the first guy you've ever met who hasn't been scared to death by your face and you're already trying to kill me. No wonder you don't have a man!&quot;</p> <p>*snickers are heard from Command's side of the radio*</p> <p><strong>Command:</strong> &quot;Get back here quick.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Right.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 returned to the Eremita's exit hatch and entered. It gave the vial to command and the Eremita resurfaced.*</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Test&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-3000's Y909 substance does not affect SCP-5144-1.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-682</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Test&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-682</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-5144-1</p> <p><strong>Cross Test:</strong> SCP-682</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> To test both SCP-5144-1 and SCP-682's immortality, they were put in a cell with instructions to terminate each other.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Test&gt;</strong></p> <p>*SCP-5144-1 enters the cell. SCP-682 is visible on the side of the room opposite to 5144-1.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP uh&#8230; 682. I am 5144-1, you can call me Mozart if you want.&quot; *5144-1 holds out hand as if to shake 682's hand*</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> *Coming closer to 5144-1* &quot;You are an interesting creature, so I will not kill you yet.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Thanks? I guess&#8230;&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;What are you?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Huh. What?&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;I said, What are you?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Oh. Hah, I don't even know. Am I a plant or animal? The day I find out, heh&#8230; that'll be the day.&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;You feel&#8230; familiar somehow. I never have met you but you still seem familiar.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hmmm. You are right, I got the same feeling I got with the slime creature. Interesting&#8230;&quot;</p> <p>*SCP-682's eyes widen*</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;How did you come into creation?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I beg your pardon?&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> *seeming slightly stressed* &quot;<em>How</em> did you come into creation?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I don't know. Kinda just woke up in the middle of the void. Why do you as-&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 is cut off by the sound of the intercom*</p> <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;Ok SCP-5144-1, please let SCP-682 attempt to terminate you.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Got it doc. *turning to 682* C'mon hit me with your best shot!&quot;</p> <p>*SCP-682 attacked 5144-1. 5144-1 did not defend itself in any way. After 3 and a half minutes of 682 tearing apart 5144-1's body, 682 stopped.*</p> <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;5144-1 you still alive?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> *Now a severed head in the corner* &quot;Yea doc I'm good.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 took 2 minutes and 53 seconds to reform.*</p> <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;Ok now, SCP-5144-1, please terminate SCP-682.&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;Ugh. Don't bother, he knows you can't kill me.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;If that's true, then I'm sorry this is gonna hurt like hell.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 raised its robotic arms and began firing its energy beams. Loud screams can be heard from 682. This went on for a continual 4 minutes of bombardment before 5144-1 ceased attack. 682 was only a charred corpse now.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> *sniffing the air* &quot;Oh no, looks like I overcooked dinner.&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;I.. I'll kill you for that!&quot;</p> <p>*682 lunged at 5144-1's leg and attempted to rip it off. However, 5144-1 leaped out of the way and then constrained 682 with its robotic arms.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Dude. You couldn't kill me in your full state, you ain't getting anything done looking like that. I guess I can try to help.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 raised its right hand to face 682. Then it started to glow blue-ish and 682's body reformed at a rate drastically quicker than normal. Finishing in only 30 seconds.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Is that better?&quot;</p> <p><strong>682:</strong> &quot;What the? How did you do that?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;One of my *holding up fingers to form quotation symbols* anomalous abilities. Not as cool as being able to bend reality but still is fun.&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-1 seems to have the same anomalous regeneration SCP-682 does. However, 5144-1's regeneration is exponentially quicker than 682's.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interaction&nbsp;of&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-999</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interaction&nbsp;of&nbsp;SCP-5144-1&nbsp;and&nbsp;SCP-999</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p>SCP-5144-1 requested to meet with SCP-999. Video footage was taken of the interaction as normal.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Recording&gt;</strong></p> <p>*SCP-5144-1 enters SCP-999's containment. No staff are present in the room. SCP-999 notices 5144-1 and squirms over to it.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Hello little guy.&quot; *5144-1 bent down to meet 999*</p> <p><strong>999:</strong> &quot;Little squeaking noises&quot;</p> <p><strong>Researcher watching interaction:</strong> &quot;Odd. It has never had a reaction like this to anyone.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Huh, I do feel better. But why do I feel like I know this guy from somewhere?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;What do you mean?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;I know for a fact I haven't met him before but he somehow seems familiar. I can't explain it. Like, something about him feels very familiar but I don't know why. It's like that feeling I had with 3k.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Researcher:</strong> &quot;3k?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;3000. The big serpent lady who makes the amnestics.&quot;</p> <p>*999 starts playing with 5144-1's tail flower, then falls back and sneezes because of the psychedelic pollen. The pollen has no effect on 999.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Heh, what a funny creature you are.&quot;</p> <p>*SCP-5144-1 continued to interact with 999, forming pieces of candy from the air and giving it to 999, for 10 minutes before leaving.*</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Recording&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Other&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Tests</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Other&nbsp;Cross&nbsp;Tests</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-173:</strong> Cross testing of SCP-5144-1 with SCP-173 to attempt to kill 5144-1 was attempted. SCP-5144-1 willingly entered the containment cell of 173 and let its neck get snapped. The test failed as 5144-1 remained alive. It was instructed to terminate the 173 clone on the spot and succeeded in vaporizing 80% of 173. This is the reason for the tremors felt throughout the site on the same day.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-4162:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was deployed in close proximity to SCP-4162 after 4162 killed a D-class. SCP-4162 designated 5144-1 as its target and began approaching it. When SCP-5144-1 was in range of 4162, its skull suddenly exploded. 10 seconds later, SCP-5144-1's skull reformed. SCP-4162 did not designate it as its target again and moved toward a D-class.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-2200-1:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was placed in SCP-2200-2's containment cell. SCP-2200-2 was instructed to attempt to terminate SCP-5144-1. After a few seconds of 2200-2 bickering, it agreed. SCP-5144-1 had its head removed by SCP-2200-1. 5144-1's head dematerialized and reformed back on its body. SCP-2200-2 was angered and attempted termination of 5144-1 three more times, all failed.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-3660:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was exposed to SCP-3660 on its forearm. Upon contact with epidermis, SCP-5144-1 claimed to feel a small itch. SCP-3660 soon opened the skin of SCP-5144-1 and then detached. An opening about 5 meters in size had formed on the forearm. SCP-5144-1 reported feeling a stinging pain before it started bleeding from the opening. No entities exited 5144-1's body during this time. SCP-5144-1 continued to bleed for 2 minutes before the opening suddenly closed.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| Cross test SCP-409:</strong> SCP-5144-1 was exposed to SCP-409. Upon contact with 409, 5144-1 reported a slight burning pain in its body. SCP-409 crystals began forming on its arm. 5 minutes into the test, SCP-5144-1's body is covered by crystals and suddenly shatters. The crystals then begin turning to dust, and SCP-5144-1 reformed from the dust particles.</p> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/774510926774403085/unknown.png" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="unknown.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>Photograph of SCP-5144-2</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-2</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> Amidias</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144-2 resides in the containment cell of SCP-5144. It is requested to stay by SCP-5144-1 but will leave if its life or another's is in danger.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5144-2 is a humanoid synthetic construct controlled by an AI. 5144-2 is about 5 feet 11 inches in height and weighs about 85kg due to its robotic buildup. The AI controls the construct as its physical body. The AI and the construct were both made by SCP-5144-1. 5144-2 can wirelessly connect to any technology within 25 meters of it, however it is loyal to 5144-1 and will cease control of technology if 5144-1 wishes it. The AI seems to have human emotions, whether made by 5144-1 or acquired on its own is unknown.</p> <p>The body resembles a white male of British descent. A mustache is visible on the face of 5144-2. 5144-2 frequently is seen wearing a fedora. It wears a tuxedo that is fused to the body of it. Attempting removal of the suit leads to the mechanical exoskeleton inside it being exposed.</p> <p><strong>Behavior:</strong> SCP-5144-2 spends most time either conversing with 5144-1 or site personnel. When not doing that, 5144-2 is connected to the internet and learning information about this reality's earth. 5144-2 claims that it has never seen earth habited before, either a barren rock or completely gone. SCP-5144-2 can survive memetic kill agents and therefor can access level 05 files in the Foundation's database. SCP-5144-1 has requested 5144-2 to not do this however, of which it has obeyed.</p> <p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> SCP-5144-2 can wirelessly connect and control any electrical devices within 25 meters of it. This includes cars, phones, computers, neural implants, etc.</p> <p>SCP-5144-2 is powered by unknown means and requires no consumption of materials or energy intake.</p> <p><strong>Addendum| Containment Breach 1:</strong> SCP-5144-2 breached containment June 27th, 20██ at 10:36 AM. It connected itself to one of the computer terminals in Site 38 and was taking in data on the Foundation, completely encrypting 05 access in milliseconds. No vital information was accessed by 5144-2. The containment breach lasted only 7 minutes before 5144-1 pulled 5144-2 away from the monitor. 5144-2 was then sent to intense therapy for 3 weeks, claiming to see in the terminal. SCP-5144-2 had apparently accessed files on SCP-1471 and located files and artwork created by those affected by 1471-A.</p> <p><strong>Interviews of SCP-5144-2:</strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5144-2| AKA: Amidias</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr. Paul Blart | Level 4 Researcher</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> After first contact was made, both SCP-5144-1 and 5144-2 were interviewed.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log, March 23rd, 20██ at 5:45 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP-5144-2. I hear you like to be called &quot;Amidias.&quot; Would you like me to call you that?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I do not care whether you call me by how my creator identifies me or not.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Ok. Now, why did you come to Earth?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;You mean this earth correct?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Yes.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Our ship was damaged and we only knew the closest planet with lifeforms was your planet.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Our?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Mozart's and mine.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Ok. How did you come into existence?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I don't fully know. Mozart tells me that one day he just got tired of not having anyone to talk to, so he decided to construct me.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Interesting. I'm guessing you are an advanced AI correct?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;That is correct.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Going back to the first question, how did your ship get damaged?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;One of the thrusters was hit by a &quot;Markus III&quot; thermonuclear warhead.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;What?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;It is a kind of weapon that humans had created in that universe.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;What year was it in that universe?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I cannot recall ever looking for that information. Sorry.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;It is ok.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;May I ask. What are you people doing?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;I beg your pardon?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I mean the SCP Foundation. The logo on your labcoat. What is the organization doing?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;I am not at liberty to give that information.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Ok then I'll find out myself.&quot;</p> <p>*SCP-5144-2's eyes started glowing green as it stared at the nearest computer terminal. Breaches in the Foundation's database firewall were detected and 5144-2 had begun accessing files. SCP-5144-2 seemed interested in database entries on many SCPs, including ones requiring level 05 access. SCP-5144-1 was called into the room to persuade 5144-2 to cease, before grabbing 5144-2 and jerking its head away from the direction of the monitor.*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;What the hell are you doing Amidias?!&quot; *5144-1 holding 5144-2 by the neck with a robotic arm*</p> <p>*5144-2 was visibly shaking*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Dude are you ok?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;These people are <em>Insane</em>!!!! So much&#8230;. the cursed things these creatures create.&quot;</p> <p>*5144-1 gave 5144-2 a quick shake*</p> <p><strong>5144-1:</strong> &quot;Start making sense ya idiot.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Don't read the 1471 log! Some things are not meant to exi&#8230; That thing those humans created&#8230; The artwork&#8230; <strong><em>Help</em></strong>!&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log, March 23rd, 20██ at 6:10 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-2 had not breached any files requiring access of 05 council. 5144-2 underwent therapy for the next 3 months. It apparently had accessed the SCP-1471 logs and seen the artwork those affected by 1471-A had created. During this time, 5144-2 harassed 2 onsite guards and begged them to terminate it, which was denied.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Interview&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <hr /> <p><strong>THE FOLLOWING LOG IS LEVEL 05 ACCESS ONLY</strong></p> <p><strong>MEMETIC KILL AGENT IMPLEMENTED</strong></p> <hr /> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> SCP-5144-2| AKA: Amidias</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Dr. Paul Blart | Level 4 Researcher</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> After failing to understand what caused the containment breach of 5144-1 and its reaction in the interview (See 5144-1 interview 4), 5144-2 was questioned.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log, October 31th, 20██ at 2:53 PM&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Hello SCP-5144-2. We have some questions about 5144-1's containment breach.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Continue.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;SCP-5144-1 seems very sensitive to the topic of his past, as well as SCP-1762. Do you know why?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Fuck. I knew it would catch up to us eventually.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;What?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Paul&#8230; are you married?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Uh, yes.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Would you do anything for them?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Yes I would. I love them.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I see. Well, let me explain how this all started. Over ten thousand years ago, me and Mozart were jumping through universes. We found this one universe where humanity had traveled to the stars and grown an empire. They were at war with other races, as human nature makes them. Me and Mozart were weapons smugglers. I thought it was dangerous but he thought it would be &quot;fun.&quot; Damn idiot didn't have to fear death like I did.</p> <p>So yea, we were smuggling weapons through enemy territory to the humans. We had gotten quite a reputation and everyone in the universe knew of us. One day, we were heading through some enemy space to meet up with our weapons dealer. We got ambushed on a heavily forested planet by the Wings of Freedom. They were a group heavily intent on stopping humans from spreading out into the stars. Like a rebellion of sorts.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;So how much had humanity taken over?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;They had grown to a population of over three trillion and spread far past the andromeda galaxy. I don't remember the exact area of space they controlled.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Interesting&#8230; Continue.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;So me and Mozart were captured by the rebellion by choice. I told the idiot that we should have just blasted our way out but he insisted that we stay and see what happens. They tossed us into an interrogation room and left us there for a few rotations. Some armed guards, not humans, came into the room on day 3 to ask us some questions. Turned out that the rebellion wanted us to work for them, to help them fight the humans. Me and Mozart talked it out and agreed to fight for them. However I soon learned why Mozart wanted to stay, damn idiot.</p> <p>Turns out he was quite&#8230; interested&#8230; in this one lifeform, the same lifeform who led the raiding party and caught us both. She was a pink ,humanoid dragon who went under the name of Sasha. I forgot to tell you, the Wings of Freedom were mostly all humanoid dragons, hence the name. That's like the plainest description I can give you, a humanoid dragon-like entity. (<em>a laugh</em>) Anyways, yea he kind of fell in love with her.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Love at first sight?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Hah, yep. So&#8230; first mission, raid and blow up a human weapons depot. The same one me and Mozart had been smuggling weapons from, so we knew the layout well. A group of 16 soldiers were dropped down. Led by Sasha, our commander, we just simply ran inside the building and started shooting at the humans. I'm guessing that Mozart didn't tell the commander about his uh&#8230; extreme usefulness in the heat of battle, because he either vaporized or trapped the humans inside in like five minutes. What we didn't expect was the reinforcements, some human had called for backup I guess.</p> <p>After the rebellion had taken most of the weapons back to the ship, a drop ship landed on the far side of the factory. At least thirty human soldiers, armed to the teeth, stormed the facility. We lost three of the group before we realized what had happened. Mozart and the commander had been cut off from the rest of the group. The rest of the group, including me, fell back to the ship and waited for the commander and Mozart. Give it a few minutes, and Mozart came barreling out of the factory wall, with Sasha on his back. They got on the ship and we took off. I'm guessing that the lovestruck idiot got the commander to notice him, perhaps&#8230; They started going on more missions together, as well as engaging in more activities together. (<em>a chuckle</em>) Mozart never used a gun before and had to learn the hard way how you have to compensate for the force launched back at you. Sasha taught him how to use a gun, make a makeshift explosive, and other weapons. Mozart shared with Sasha the stories of me and him traveling the cosmos.</p> <p>Over the next six years, him and Sasha were practically everywhere together. Including many nights where I would leave them in their quarters to&#8230; have fun&#8230; You know what I mean.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Ah I understand.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Yea. It was kind of living the dream for them. Well, until that day&#8230;&quot;</p> <p>*5144-2 started staring at the floor*</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Amidias, you there?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Yes sorry. That day&#8230; the day it all went to shit. One final mission it was thought, one final mission to deal enough damage to the human race. The point of this mission was to obtain a data chip with information that&#8230; goddamnit I sound like I'm parodying Star Wars ain't I?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Yes it sounds like it a bit.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Well, I am not joking around with this. Anyway, the mission was to collect a data chip with information on the human goal, to spread to the farthest reaches of the universe. As well as the proof of what they do to planets when they leave them. The point was to get the data and send it out to every race to let them know what humanity was doing, and hopefully turn everybody on the humans.</p> <p>An attack squad of five ships of twenty soldiers each. Led by Sasha and her right hand lieutenant, Mozart. The ships landed in a hangar of the facility that housed the data and immediately were met with resistance from the humans. Speed up some futuristic firefight and a lot of damage to my audio sensors, we got into the facility, grabbed the data chip, and were on our way out. Four of the ships had made it out, leaving me waiting for the commander's group.</p> <p>Only Sasha and Mozart, in their group, survived. I saw them running toward the ship with Sasha carrying the data. They had almost reached it when&#8230;&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Amidias you there dude? If it's too much I can wait till later to get the rest.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;No. No, I can't keep it a secret any longer.</p> <p>They had almost reached the ship when Sasha was hit square in the back by a bullet. I heard her cry out in pain and looked outside the ship to see what had happened. Mozart held Sasha in his arms in the middle of the hangar. I barely heard her say to him &quot;Thank you for this life.&quot; before she gave him a kiss, then went limp. I scanned her body and&#8230; she had died. The bullet had severed her spinal cord.</p> <p>Then for the next few minutes, Mozart sat there crying with Sasha's body in his arms. Armed human guards soon circled him and warned him to surrender or they would shoot. Then, he stood up and said five words. &quot;You did this to her.&quot; The energy orb in his chest started to glow a dark red as well as his eyes. A wreath of red fire covered his body. The ground started to shake and dust began swirling around his feet, then all the guards started screaming in pain before turning to dust. But&#8230; it didn't stop there.</p> <p>He opened a portal and walked through it. To where specifically it went, I do not know. But I soon learned what he did.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Continue?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Genocide. Genocide on a cosmic scale. Whatever was controlling him, it raised his hand to the roof of the building, and in his fiery rage, he fired a massive burst of energy into the night sky. Then&#8230; the end.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;What do you mean the end?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;It was like a chain reaction, that burst of light fired off into the sky and started igniting every single star, planet, and black hole. An insane person would compare it to connecting dots in the sky, but the dots don't explode with the force of a fucking supernova.&quot;</p> <p>*Dr. Blart is now sitting on the edge of their chair*</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;For 44 seconds, that's how long it took. 44 seconds for the chain reaction to swallow every single planet, star, and black hole in the cosmos. There was nothing left&#8230; nothing. I and whatever was controlling Mozart, we were the last 2 living beings in that universe. Just a black void that was once a beautiful night sky. Just a void.</p> <p>Then he stopped, the fire around him had died, he kneeled in front of Sasha's body, stopped glowing red, and passed out. Probably from the energy he emitted. (<em>sigh</em>) I moved Sasha's body outside and gave her a burial. Then dragged Mozart into the ship. I tried to undo what had happened. I knew I couldn't wipe his memory, so I just suppressed some of it. I used a makeshift neural link to digitally enter his mind and alter it. I suppressed his memory of Sasha's death. Above it, I added fake memories of them succeeding in the mission and stopping the spread of humanity.</p> <p>When he awoke, three months later, I had set up a fake story. That the rebellion succeeded in stopping the humans. I made fake messages from Sasha to Mozart that they had left this universe to go to another one. There was a massive gap in his memory, and I convinced him that he just got drunk at a bar last night. He somehow bought it, and we left that barren universe on the fake quest to find Sasha.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Oh&#8230; Jesus Christ. But that doesn't fully explain why he broke containment.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I believe that, the 1762 records subconsciously brought back the memory of Sasha's death, just for a second.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;That makes more sense.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;Paul, you guys here at the Foundation handle some scary things. Things that could end the world with the snap of their fingers. But this, this is something different. I don't know what it is&#8230; One thing is clear, Mozart <em>cannot</em> remember Sasha's death! Do you understand?&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Yes I do.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> <em>sigh</em> &quot;I&#8230; I fear I've only made things worse.&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Huh?&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;I mean, what if I never suppressed his memories? Maybe he would have gotten over her dea-&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;Amidias, I think you did the right thing.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;But&#8230; what if all that anger is growing inside him? What if he breaks again? Paul, Mozart must <em><strong>never</strong></em> remember Sasha's death! If he does, he&#8230; he will make an XK class End of the World scenario look like a fucking tea party!&quot;</p> <p><strong>Paul:</strong> &quot;I understand.&quot;</p> <p><strong>5144-2:</strong> &quot;The worst part, he was going to propose to her after the mission. He told me that he was going to propose to her after they made it back to the safety of the rebellion. Why&#8230; why did that bullet have to land!&quot;</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> SCP-5144-1 has shown the same immense power like it did during the containment breach once before. It seems that 5144-1 underwent great mental trauma in the past and the trauma was suppressed by technology that SCP-5144-2 used.</p> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/778471470644723773/unknown.png" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="unknown.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>Image of SCP-5144-3 taken by satellite</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-3</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> The Star Jumper</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144-3 is contained at Site-38 in SCP-5144's cell. It is an inanimate object and is easily contained. However its size was the determining factor in 5144's containment cell size.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> 5144-3 is a large spaceship around ██ by ██ by ██ meters in size. This is why the containment cell is 100 by 50 by 40 meters in size. Whatever the ship is constructed of is too durable for any non-anomalous foundation weaponry to damage. However, 5144-3 has visible scorch marks and damage to its right thrusters and hull (See SCP-5144-1 interview for details).</p> <p><strong>Bottom level:</strong> Located near the rear of the ship is the cargo bay door. Inside the cargo bay are metal crates of unknown &quot;fruits&quot; described 5144-1. The airlock opens directly into the bridge of the ship. In the center of the bridge is a 15 meter tall pedestal. Atop the pedestal is an open platform ,that 5144-1 has shown, activates a spherical hologram when 5144-1 is present. The hologram has the ability to detect 5144-1's thoughts and movements, moving exactly how he wishes it to. The hologram sphere glows a light blue and vaguely resembles an advanced computer setup. Ship diagnostics and status checks are visible on the hologram.</p> <p><strong>Top level:</strong>On the sides of the bridge are metal grate steps leading to the top of the ship. Up in the top level, there is a balcony overviewing the bridge and is about 3 feet higher then the command platform. A large nuclear reactor is visibly exposed in the center of the top area, also glowing a light blue but substantially brighter in comparison to the control hologram. On the walls around the reactor are many lockers each containing different items. (See list of items below) In the rear top level of the ship was a single metal door opening into a hallway that connected to a bedroom, a spare bedroom, a bathroom, and a charging station for 5144-2.</p> <p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> SCP-5144-3 is a vehicle from another universe. The technology used in its construction is greatly evolved.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">List&nbsp;of&nbsp;sub-anomalous&nbsp;items&nbsp;in&nbsp;SCP-5144-3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">List&nbsp;of&nbsp;sub-anomalous&nbsp;items&nbsp;in&nbsp;SCP-5144-3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">The items below are identified as SCP-5144-3[A-Z]</span></strong></p> <p><strong>5144-3A:</strong> Twenty cans of an unknown meat substance.</p> <p><strong>5144-3B:</strong> An unopened wine bottle from [REDACTED] Winery, which does not exist.</p> <p><strong>5144-3C:</strong> 3 World War 2 grade grenades. (Confiscated)</p> <p><strong>5144-3D:</strong> A videotape of a foundation worker trapped on the moon after SCP-2399 destroyed earth.</p> <p><strong>5144-3E:</strong> An Aztec ritual dagger with blood of Roman Emperor Caesar on it. (Confiscated)</p> <p><strong>5144-3F:</strong> A photo album of SCP-5144-1 and a pink, humanoid entity.</p> <p><strong>5144-3G:</strong> 7 liters of nutrient rich water.</p> <p><strong>5144-3H:</strong> A sack of 37 coins with unknown etchings on them. SCP-5144-1 describes them as an alien currency.</p> <p><strong>5144-3I:</strong> A small mirror that reflects an x-ray image of a user.</p> <p><strong>5144-3J:</strong> A handgun, mechanical in nature, not resembling any model known. Handgun fires .50 caliber bullets without recoil. (SCP-5144-1 denied confiscation of item)</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"></div> <hr /> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/777271906080129054/unknown.png" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="unknown.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>Artwork of SCP-5144-4 by Anne Bookevich</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-4</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> The Archway</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Safe</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5144-4 is to be contained inside a perimeter fence approximately 2.3 kilometers from the structure and surrounding it completely. Guards are to patrol the perimeter fence at all times to stop any unauthorized entrance.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5144-4 is a large marble structure of circular shape and 2 kilometers in diameter with a height of 3 kilometers. 5144-4 was created by a containment breach of SCP-5144-1 when 5144-1 formed it using the surrounding landscape(See 5144-1 containment breach and abilities).</p> <p>SCP-5144-4's exterior is a marble structure with no viewpoints inside. On the western side of the structure is the entrance, a 90 meter high by 40 meter wide archway. Above the archway etched in the marble reads &quot;████ ██ ███████.&quot; The interior of the structure is lit by floating lanterns visible around the structure at varying heights. The walls have engravings of unknown lifeforms and locations on them. Water is also seen seeping from holes in the walls to create pools. Roof of the structure has clouds that form randomly by unknown means.</p> <p>Between the center of the structure and the entrance is a pedestal with SCP-1762 located atop. 1762 is openable but all attempts to remove it have failed. In the direct center of SCP-5144-4 is an identical archway to the entrance. When a living creature is within 36 meters of it, the archway will start to shimmer and generate light. If a living creature passes through the archway, they are teleported to an identical structure but without water flowing from the walls or lanterns lighting it. Where the entrance should be located is instead a solid wall of sandstone.</p> <p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> SCP-5144-4 is a gateway to another reality (SCP-5144-5).</p> <p>SCP-5144-4 will not let SCP-1762 be removed from the pedestal inside it.</p> <p>SCP-5144-4 does not allow radio contact between different sides of the portal.</p> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"></div> </div> <hr /> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"><img src="https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/750525450379460610/777257660340109352/Screenshot_2020-11-14_124151.jpg" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;" alt="Screenshot_2020-11-14_124151.jpg" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:WIDTH-GOES-HERE;"> <p>SCP-5144-5 viewed from top of rock formation</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5144-5</p> <p><strong>AKA:</strong> The Fallen Fantasy</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> No unauthorized personnel are allowed to enter SCP-5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5144-5 is an unknown reality or world connected to ours by SCP-5144-4, which was created by SCP-5144-1. 5144-5 is the landscape outside of the 5144-4 structure on that side. Access to 5144-5 is only accessible via a drilled tunnel from exit of 5144-4 to the surface. SCP-5144-5 seems to have one star it orbits, and 2 moons that orbit it. Time functions similar in 5144-5 as it does on earth. The day/night cycle seems consistent with Earth's.</p> <p>The explored part of 5144-5 was once habited by seemingly intelligent lifeforms. The surrounding 5-7 kilometers from the shaft exit resembles a desert. Outside of that is a forest, not resembling any flora on earth, that looks to have recently survived a forest fire. In the distance, a large mountain range is visible with 30% of it being held aloft by anomalous means.</p> <p>SCP-5144-5 is mostly void of life in the explored sector. However, large wormlike entities are visible burrowing under the sand. Entities flee when loud noises above 150 decibels are emitted. Entities have armored plating that requires explosives to break through. No other living entities are documented in the explored sector.</p> <p><strong>Anomalous Properties:</strong> It is an alternate reality with unknown threats.</p> <p><strong>Exploration Logs of 5144-5:</strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Mission Objective:</strong> Explore the surface of SCP-5144-5</p> <p><strong>Preparations:</strong> Mining attempts on the other side of SCP-5144-4 recently broke through to the surface. D-20317, a male in his late 30s charged with homicide, was sent to the surface. D-20317 was given 1 days worth of food and water, a 9 millimeter pistol, a compass, a military knife, a head mounted camera, and a field kit.</p> <p>Researcher Linda Brooke was put in-charge of the exploration of SCP-5144-5. 5144-2 has requested to observe the exploration alongside Ms. Brooke. The request was accepted. Ms. Brooke, SCP-5144-2, and 2 armed MTF made camp inside SCP-5144-4. Due to SCP-5144-5's anomalous time altering abilities, the camp had to be constructed on the opposite side of the Archway to that of Earth.</p> <p><strong>Mission Log:</strong> D-20317 was deployed at exit point of the mining shaft. Class-D said they noticed a desert-like landscape surrounding them. D-20317 took samples of the sand, remarking that there were many white chips in the sand. Class-D said that there are large boulder-like rock formations spread around the landscape, as well as dead trees scattered around. Video footage shows the trees not resembling any flora native to Earth. D-20317 turns the camera to the sky to view a sun with a yellow-ish orange hue. Class-D was instructed to pull out compass, of which they did. The compass did not function properly, instead spinning around rapidly.</p> <p>Linda Brooke asked the Class-D, via radio, if they noticed any structures nearby. D-20317 claims to see some large floating mountains in the distance. The video footage showed a mountain range with at least 30% of the mountains suspended in the air by unknown means. D-20317 was instructed to attempt to climb one of the large sandstone boulders to get a better vantage point. Class-D began running toward the closest boulder when they claimed to have felt a shaking in the ground.</p> <p>SCP-5144-2 noticed something in the video feed, a large mound of sand moving at high speed toward the D-class. D-20317 was instructed to return to the mining shaft. Class-D began sprinting to the shaft but tripped on a large white rock protruding from the sand. The video camera was dislodged from the helmet on D-20317 when they tripped and fell. The footage shows Class-D firing off 3 shots with the 9mm at the mound of sand. A large wormlike entity burst out of the sand and consumed the D-class before burrowing back into the ground.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Mission Objective:</strong> Explore surface of SCP-5144-5. Reclaim supplies and samples carried by D-20317.</p> <p><strong>Secondary Objective:</strong> Capture and study wormlike entity if possible.</p> <p><strong>Preparations:</strong> Level 2 Scientists Anton and Mikkel Schmidt and MTF Cadet Rosaline Jenson were sent to the surface of SCP-5144-5. Anton was given a field kit, a liter of water, 7 energy bars, a knife, and a flashlight. Mikkel was given a head mounted camera, sample flasks, an emergency flare, and a 9 millimeter pistol. Rose was armed with a FN P90, a concussion grenade, 5 clips of ammunition, and a lighter.</p> <p><strong>Mission Log:</strong> Anton and Mikkel arrived on time. Rosaline 5 minutes later. The group entered the mining shaft and began their ascent. Once reaching the surface, Cadet Rose says that it is currently nighttime on 5144-5. Camera footage shows 2 moons orbiting the planet. No familiar stars or constellations are visible. Mikkel obtained what was left of D-20317's supplies; the camera, field kit, and backpack. They placed the items inside the opening of the mining shaft. Anton examines the white rock D-20317 tripped over and finds a vaguely human skull. Skull is placed in field kit.</p> <p>MTF Cadet Rose claims to have felt a rumbling in the ground. Mikkel and Anton agree. After 26 seconds of rumblings, the wormlike entity attempted to burrow under Rosaline and consume them. The cadet jumped out of the way and avoided the attack. Rose and Mikkel begin firing upon the entity and cause it to begin fleeing. Scientist Anton grabbed the concussion grenade from the MTF's belt and threw it at the entity. The grenade explodes and the creature ceases movement. Rosaline unloads a clip of ammunition into the body to confirm termination. Anton proceeded to use his knife to cut open the entity's abdomen to extract samples of blood and tissue. The entity bleeds a yellow liquid.</p> <p>Mikkel requests the group return to SCP-5144-4, but is denied. The team is instructed to gain a vantage point on top one of the large sandstone formations. Cadet Rosaline takes the video camera from Anton and begins scaling one of the larger boulders. Once reaching the top, Rose holds the camera in the air and slowly circles around. Camera footage catches the &quot;floating&quot; mountain range, a large white rock formation, and a burnt forest obscuring a structure. The group are instructed to return to SCP-5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Post-Mission Data:</strong> The samples of the sand show the white chips to be shards of glass. The discovered skull seems to be human in size, however having a larger brain case and more accentuated jaw. Tests on the wormlike entities' blood and tissue do not give indication of any relation to lifeforms native to earth.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;3</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Mission Objective:</strong> Explore SCP-5144-5. Reach and infiltrate structure located inside forest about 3 kilometers from exit point of 5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Secondary objective:</strong> Locate intelligent life.</p> <p><strong>Preparations:</strong> MTF Lambda-5 (&quot;White Rabbits&quot;) are prepared for traveling across SCP-5144-5 toward a structure sighted inside a forest roughly2 kilometers from 5144-4. Researcher Linda Brooke and SCP-5144-2 will remain in radio contact with the MTF squad back at SCP-5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Mission Log:</strong> MTF Lambda-5 deployed at exit point of 5144-4 and began traversing across the desert-like landscape. The squad took 29 minutes of walking through the desert region before reaching the forest. Many of the MTF describe the forest as being &quot;long dead&quot; and &quot;scorched&quot;. The trees, in the video footage, are seemingly charred. Trees are about 2 to 2.5 meters wide. No leaves are present on the trees. The squadron also claims to see a low fog drifting across the forest floor.</p> <p>MTF reach the structure 36 minutes after deployment. The structure seems to be not one, but many house shaped buildings constructed in the canopy of the trees. Lambda-5 located a wooden stairway near the base of one of the trees and began their ascent. When reaching the top, a path of boards connecting the buildings in the trees are all connected to the single stairway tree. Most of the paths are damaged and not crossable, however the group find one and follow it to the building it's connected to. Video footage shows the structure having wooden shingles on the roof, glass windows, and a large door 2.2 meters tall. The windows of the structure are shattered.</p> <p>The MTF entered the building to find 2 chairs, a table, a large bed, and some crates in the corner. All the items inside the building are slightly large for a human to use. All items are also slightly burnt. Sitting in one of the chairs is a 6.5 foot tall skeleton, blackened from exposure to flame. Another skeleton, 6.7, was found on the floor near the bed. 2 digits from the hands of each skeleton were collected as samples. Video footage shows the skeleton skulls resembling the same skull found during SCP-5144-5 exploration mission 1.</p> <p>After inspection, the skeleton on the floor seems to have been holding a small box. The box was placed inside a field kit. Further inspection shows the crates in the corner to be filled with unknown foodstuffs, as well as fabric and possible items or weaponry. The objects are damaged by fire way too much to be confirmed. The squadron left the structure and returned to the forest floor. MTF Lambda-5 were instructed to return to SCP-5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Post-Mission Data:</strong> Examination of the small box shows the contents not to be damaged by fire. The contents were as follows. A small feather with an insertion at the tip, possible use as a pen. Dried black liquid, suggested to be ink. And a piece of paper with the following text on it. The text is surprisingly in English. Some of the message is damaged and unreadable.</p> <p><em>Dear Family,</em></p> <p><em>Anahita and I will return to you soon. We are finishing our work</em> [Damaged] <em>and will be back for the journey to the new land. Please prepare for the journey when we arrive, we cannot waste time. They are burying the room in a fort night. We will reach you before</em> [Damaged]. <em>Good travels.</em></p> <p><em>love,</em><br /> [Damaged]</p> <p>The letter refers to the burying of a &quot;room&quot; and a family traveling to a &quot;new land&quot;. Sadly there is not enough information to understand what happened.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;4</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;4</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Mission Objective:</strong> Set up temporary/ permanent base of operations on surface of SCP-5144-5.<br /> <strong>Target Location:</strong> Large white rock formation.<br /> <strong>Estimated time:</strong> 8 hours.</p> <p><strong>Preparations:</strong> A group consisting of 3 scientists and 7 members of the MTF Lambda-5 unit were deployed at the surface of SCP-5144-5. Each member has 2 days worth of food and water, as well as a fold up tent and matches. All scientists are also given a field kit each to collect samples. Radio contact is kept between the exploration team and basecamp inside SCP-5144-4.</p> <p><strong>Mission Log:</strong></p> <p>-Day 1-</p> <p>The exploration team was deployed at the exit point of the mining shaft connecting SCP-5144-4 to the surface of 5144-5. The group began traversing the desert landscape in the direction of the large rock formation. 1 hour of traveling, the group encountered another wormlike entity like was encountered during the first and second exploration missions. Entity was terminated, no casualties reported.</p> <p>The exploration team, about 3 hours into the journey, claim to have spotted a large flying object in the sky. Camera footage shows a large bird-like entity, estimated 9 meters tall, with red feathers, flying high above the group. The entity flew closer and landed on a sandstone boulder roughly 30 meters from the group. It began hitting the boulder it stood on with its large beak. The noise seems to have alerted one of the worm creatures, which began burrowing underground toward the boulder. The bird entity flew into the air and dove at the moving sand mound, spraying sand over the group. Camera footage was temporarily lost. After the team recovered, footage shows the bird entity back on the boulder consuming the worm. One of the MTF cadets made a joke about &quot;the early bird getting the worm&quot; which made some of the group laugh. Exploration team continued travel.</p> <p>The team reached the large white rock form in 4 hours and 34 minutes. The rock formation is actually a massive skeletal structure about 200 meters long. The form looks vaguely similar to a lizard skeleton, however distinct horns are found on the back of the skull. The skeletal structure is damaged, with breaks in the ribcage and spine visible. 2 unknown appendages, possibly secondary arms, are located near the midsection of the entity. Scientists Anton and Mikkel Schmidt took samples of the bone. The team locate the skull of the deceased organism and make camp inside the open jaw of it. The maw of the creature is forced open by a large boulder that has broken half of the jaw on the right side. Evidence suggests the entity fell on the boulder and shattered its jaw on impact, however was probably dead before impact. One of the MTF noticed the sun setting in 5144-5 and started a small fire inside the skull. The group were instructed to rest for the next day. 2 MTF cadets held watch at the front of the skull.</p> <p>-Day 2-</p> <p>The group were awoken around 5:00 AM, in 5144-5, to the sound of thunder. Video footage showed a large storm coming toward the desert area from the &quot;floating&quot; mountain range. The storm itself seemed that of a thunderstorm. However when lightning would strike, a large &quot;tornado&quot;, as one scientist described it, of lightning would strike the ground for approximately 32 seconds. The group are warned to stay inside the skull of the deceased organism until the storm passes. Radio contact was lost for 6 hours when the storm got between the camp at 5144-4 and the team in the field.</p> <p>-Day 3-</p> <p>Radio contact was restored. The storm had passed. The exploration group had begun rationing out food and water and were preparing to return to 5144-4. Level 3 Researcher, Linda Brooke, at 5144-4 gave them permission to return. The team returned to the exit shaft of 5144-4 in 3 hours and 59 minutes.</p> <p><strong>Post-Mission Data:</strong> Chemical analysis does not show any connection from the deceased organism to that of Earthly life. The next few weeks after the mission, an airlock was constructed at the exit point of the mining shaft. 2 more missions to the skeleton structure camp were sent with supplies to reinforce the camp and make it more suitable for long-term survival. These missions did not have any significance and the logs were discarded.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;5</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;log&nbsp;5</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>Mission Objective:</strong> Long term exploration mission.<br /> <strong>Target Location:</strong> &quot;Floating&quot; Mountain range.<br /> <strong>Estimated time:</strong> Unknown.</p> <p><strong>Preparations:</strong> A group of 3 scientists, Anton and Mikkel Schmidt and Mary Williams, and 2 members of MTF unit Lamdba-5, Rosaline Jenson and Jim Williams, were sent from the skeleton basecamp in the direction of the mountain range. Each scientist was armed with a field kit, a military knife, a 9 millimeter pistol with 5 clips of ammo, a box of matches, and a fold up tent. Each MTF were armed with FM-P90s, 2 concussion grenades each, a military knife, 20 clips of P90 ammunition, a box of matches, and a fold up tent. Furthermore, the group were given 3 horses for travel. The group was also given 3 months worth of food and 4 weeks of water. Snow is visible on the mountains, so it suggests water will be there. Finally, the group was also given one video camera to log their findings if they are to return.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><strong>Mission Log:</strong></span></p> <p><em>This mission is currently ongoing. Radio contact was lost near the base of the mountain range. No recovery teams have been sent as of yet.</em></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"></div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wolfmandeth" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6859403&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606767351" alt="Wolfmandeth" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6859403)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wolfmandeth" >Wolfmandeth</a></span></p> 
				 	]]>
